tion-colon-ref-short with optional detail\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow commit is created\n    When: item reference is available\n    Then: commit message includes ULID prefix (8 chars) or primary slug\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow is not configured (no worktree)\n    When: command that would normally commit runs\n    Then: command completes successfully without attempting git operations\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: save operation fails\n    When: validation or IO error occurs\n    Then: no commit is attempted and error is returned\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow has remote configured\n    When: commit succeeds\n    Then: push is attempted in fire-and-forget mode (failure doesn't block command)\n  [ac-7] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: commit or push fails\n    When: save succeeded but git operation failed\n    Then: command succeeds but outputs warning about sync state\n  [ac-8] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: command performs multiple related saves\n    When: all saves complete successfully\n    Then: single atomic commit covers all changes\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-localhost-security ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-localhost-security)\n    Given: server is starting\n    When: binding to network interface\n    Then: only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-localhost-security)\n    Given: connection attempt from non-localhost\n    When: request received\n    Then: connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-localhost-security)\n    Given: server is configured\n    When: configuration allows external binding\n    Then: warning displayed about security implications\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-websocket-protocol ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: WebSocket connection is established\n    When: client connects\n    Then: server assigns unique connection ID and sends connected event with session_id\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: client wants notifications\n    When: subscribe command sent with topics array\n    Then: server tracks subscription and sends ack with request_id\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: client is subscribed to topic\n    When: relevant change occurs\n    Then: server broadcasts event with format {msg_id, seq, timestamp, topic, event, data}\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: WebSocket connection is active\n    When: 30 seconds pass without activity\n    Then: server sends ping frame\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: ping was sent\n    When: no pong received within 90 seconds\n    Then: connection is closed with code 1001\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: server sends events\n    When: client cannot keep up (backpressure)\n    Then: server pauses non-critical broadcasts until drain event\n  [ac-7] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: connection is closing\n    When: close initiated\n    Then: use code 1000 for clean close, 1001 for timeout, 1011 for error\n  [ac-8] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: client reconnects after disconnect\n    When: new connection established\n    Then: client resets sequence tracking (lastSeqProcessed = -1) since server generates new sequence"}}]}}}
./sessions/01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP/events.jsonl:{"ts":1769161525474,"seq":18568,"type":"session.update","session_id":"01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP","data":{"iteration":10,"update":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"toolResponse":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Run /local-review for PR #185. Check AC coverage, test quality, E2E preference, and test isolation.","agentId":"acaa519","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Local Review Report for PR #185\n\nI've completed the local review for PR #185 against the `@daemon-server` spec. Here's the comprehensive analysis:\n\n---\n\n## 1. AC Coverage Analysis - CRITICAL ISSUES FOUND\n\n### Implemented ACs (with test coverage):\n- **ac-1**: Server starts on configurable port ✓ (2 tests)\n- **ac-2**: Binds to localhost only ✓ (1 test)\n- **ac-3**: Rejects non-localhost with 403 ✓ (2 tests)\n- **ac-11**: Health endpoint implementation ✓ (1 test)\n- **ac-12**: Graceful shutdown on SIGTERM/SIGINT ✓ (3 tests)\n- **ac-15**: Plugin pattern for middleware ✓ (2 tests)\n\n### Missing AC Coverage (MUST-FIX):\nThe spec has **16 direct ACs** plus multiple inherited ACs from traits. The PR only covers **6 out of 16 core ACs**. Missing ACs include:\n\n- **ac-4**: File watching with WebSocket broadcast (not implemented)\n- **ac-5**: Debouncing rapid changes (not implemented)\n- **ac-6**: Error handling for YAML parse errors (not implemented)\n- **ac-7**: Recovery with exponential backoff (not implemented)\n- **ac-8**: Fallback to Chokidar (partial - dependency added, not implemented)\n- **ac-9**: Daemon mode with PID file (not implemented)\n- **ac-10**: Stop command (not implemented)\n- **ac-13**: WebSocket ping after 30s inactivity (not implemented)\n- **ac-14**: Close connection after 90s no pong (not implemented)\n- **ac-16**: Bun compile to standalone (not tested)\n\n**Inherited trait ACs** also lack coverage:\n- **@trait-json-output**: 6 ACs (not applicable yet - no JSON mode)\n- **@trait-error-guidance**: 6 ACs (not applicable yet - no error handling)\n- **@trait-shadow-commit**: 8 ACs (not applicable - server doesn't modify shadow)\n- **@trait-localhost-security**: 3 ACs (partially covered by ac-3, but ac-3 from trait mentions warning about external binding config)\n- **@trait-websocket-protocol**: 8 ACs (not implemented)\n\n---\n\n## 2. Test Quality - CRITICAL ISSUES FOUND\n\n### Fluff Tests Identified (MUST-FIX):\n\n**ALL 15 tests in this PR are fluff tests.** They check for implementation details (code structure) rather than actual behavior. Here's the breakdown:\n\n#### Tests that only check for string presence in source code:\n\n1. **Lines 49-60**: Checks `package.json` has Elysia dependency\n   - **Why fluff**: Would pass even if server doesn't work\n   - **Fix needed**: Actually start server, verify it responds on port 3456\n\n2. **Lines 62-72**: Checks index.ts contains `--port=` string\n   - **Why fluff**: Would pass even if flag does nothing\n   - **Fix needed**: Start server with custom port, verify it binds to that port\n\n3. **Lines 74-86**: Checks server.ts contains string 'localhost'\n   - **Why fluff**: String presence doesn't prove binding behavior\n   - **Fix needed**: Try connecting from non-localhost, verify rejection\n\n4. **Lines 88-100**: Checks middleware function name exists\n   - **Why fluff**: Function could exist but not work\n   - **Fix needed**: Make actual HTTP request from non-localhost IP, verify 403\n\n5. **Lines 102-112**: Checks Host header validation code exists\n   - **Why fluff**: Code presence doesn't prove validation works\n   - **Fix needed**: Send requests with different Host headers, verify behavior\n\n6. **Lines 114-127**: Checks health endpoint string exists in source\n   - **Why fluff**: Endpoint could exist but return wrong data\n   - **Fix needed**: Make GET request to /api/health, verify JSON structure\n\n7. **Lines 129-140**: Checks SIGTERM string exists in code\n   - **Why fluff**: Handler could exist but not work\n   - **Fix needed**: Start server, send SIGTERM, verify graceful shutdown\n\n8. **Lines 142-152**: Checks SIGINT string exists in code\n   - **Why fluff**: Same issue as SIGTERM\n   - **Fix needed**: Start server, send SIGINT, verify graceful shutdown\n\n9. **Lines 154-164**: Checks `app.server?.stop()` exists in code\n   - **Why fluff**: Code could exist but fail at runtime\n   - **Fix needed**: Verify server actually stops when signal sent\n\n10. **Lines 166-179**: Checks 'cors' string exists\n    - **Why fluff**: Import doesn't prove CORS works\n    - **Fix needed**: Make CORS preflight request, verify headers\n\n11. **Lines 181-188**: Checks package.json has CORS dependency\n    - **Why fluff**: Dependency presence doesn't prove configuration\n    - **Fix needed**: Actual CORS request verification\n\n12. **Lines 190-197**: Checks chokidar dependency exists\n    - **Why fluff**: Dependency doesn't prove fallback logic\n    - **Fix needed**: Test file watching works or falls back\n\n13. **Lines 199-208**: Checks `.ws(` string exists\n    - **Why fluff**: WebSocket code presence doesn't prove it works\n    - **Fix needed**: Establish WebSocket connection, verify events\n\n14. **Lines 210-219**: Checks `--daemon` string in index.ts\n    - **Why fluff**: Flag presence doesn't prove daemon mode works\n    - **Fix needed**: Start in daemon mode, verify process detaches and PID file created\n\n15. **Lines 221-231**: Checks function signature exists\n    - **Why fluff**: Signature doesn't prove function works\n    - **Fix needed**: Call createServer, verify it returns working server\n\n### Why This is a Problem:\n\n**The litmus test failure**: None of these tests would fail if:\n- Server doesn't start\n- Port binding fails\n- Localhost enforcement breaks\n- Health endpoint returns wrong data\n- Shutdown handlers don't work\n- CORS headers are missing\n\nThese tests verify **\"code exists\"** not **\"feature works\"**.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Test Strategy - NEEDS IMPROVEMENT\n\n### Current Strategy:\n- **0% E2E tests**: No actual server startup or HTTP requests\n- **100% source code inspection**: All tests just read files and check strings\n\n### Recommended Strategy:\n\n**E2E tests should:**\n```typescript\n// GOOD: Test actual behavior\nit('should start server on default port 3456', async () => {\n  // Start actual server\n  const server = spawn('bun', ['run', 'daemon'], { cwd: tempDir });\n  \n  // Wait for server ready\n  await waitForPort(3456);\n  \n  // Make real HTTP request\n  const response = await fetch('http://127.0.0.1:3456/api/health');\n  expect(response.status).toBe(200);\n  \n  const data = await response.json();\n  expect(data).toHaveProperty('status', 'ok');\n  expect(data).toHaveProperty('uptime');\n  \n  // Cleanup\n  server.kill('SIGTERM');\n});\n\n// GOOD: Test rejection behavior\nit('should reject non-localhost with 403', async () => {\n  const server = spawn('bun', ['run', 'daemon'], { cwd: tempDir });\n  await waitForPort(3456);\n  \n  // Send request with non-localhost Host header\n  const response = await fetch('http://127.0.0.1:3456/api/health', {\n    headers: { 'Host': 'evil.com' }\n  });\n  \n  expect(response.status).toBe(403);\n  const data = await response.json();\n  expect(data.error).toBe('Forbidden');\n  \n  server.kill('SIGTERM');\n});\n```\n\n**Unit tests are acceptable for:**\n- Complex validation logic in isolation\n- Helper functions\n- Middleware functions (when tested with mock contexts)\n\nBut for a server implementation, **E2E tests are strongly preferred** because they prove the feature actually works for users.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Test Isolation - PASS\n\n### Analysis:\n✓ All tests use `createTempDir()` in `beforeEach`\n✓ All tests clean up with `cleanupTempDir()` in `afterEach`\n✓ Git repo initialized in temp dir, not kspec repo\n✓ Fixtures copied to temp dir via `setupTempFixtures()`\n\n**However**, the tests don't actually run in temp dirs - they read source files from the project directory:\n```typescript\n// Lines 51-52, 66-67, 77-78, etc.\nawait readFile(join(process.cwd(), 'packages/daemon/...'), 'utf-8')\n```\n\nThis is acceptable for these \"source inspection\" tests, but **real E2E tests MUST run the server from tempDir**:\n```typescript\n// Correct: Run from temp dir\nconst server = spawn('bun', ['run', 'daemon'], { cwd: tempDir });\n\n// Wrong: Run from project dir\nconst server = spawn('bun', ['run', 'daemon']);\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Summary of Blocking Issues\n\n### MUST-FIX (Blocking):\n\n1. **Missing AC Coverage**: Only 6/16 core ACs have any tests at all. The PR claims to implement ac-3 and ac-12, but the spec has 14 other ACs that are completely untested.\n\n2. **All Tests are Fluff**: Every single test just checks if strings exist in source code. None verify actual behavior. Would pass even if server doesn't work.\n\n3. **No E2E Tests**: No actual server startup, no real HTTP requests, no behavior validation.\n\n### Advisory:\n\n4. **Partial Implementation**: The PR correctly implements ac-3 (localhost enforcement) and ac-12 (graceful shutdown), but the scope doesn't match the full spec. This is acceptable IF the task scope was limited to just these ACs.\n\n---\n\n## Recommendations\n\n### Option 1: Fix Tests for Current Scope (Recommended)\nIf the task was only to implement ac-3 and ac-12:\n\n1. **Replace all 15 fluff tests** with 4-5 real E2E tests:\n   - Server starts and responds on default port\n   - Custom port works via --port flag\n   - Non-localhost Host header returns 403\n   - Localhost variations (127.0.0.1, ::1) work\n   - SIGTERM/SIGINT trigger graceful shutdown\n\n2. **Add AC annotations** to match the actual scope:\n   ```typescript\n   // AC: @daemon-server ac-3\n   it('should reject non-localhost with 403', async () => { ... });\n   ```\n\n3. **Run real server** in tests using Bun runtime\n\n### Option 2: Expand Scope to Match Spec\nIf the goal is to complete the full daemon-server spec:\n\n1. Implement missing ACs (ac-4 through ac-14, ac-16)\n2. Write E2E tests for each AC\n3. Add AC annotations for traceability\n\n---\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/tests/daemon-server.test.ts` (233 lines)\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/src/server.ts` (127 lines)\n- Spec: `@daemon-server` (16 core ACs + 31 inherited trait ACs)\n\n---\n\n**Verdict**: **MUST-FIX before merge**. All tests need to be replaced with real E2E tests that verify actual behavior, not source code structure."}],"totalDurationMs":96801,"totalTokens":32255,"totalToolUseCount":9,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":262,"cache_read_input_tokens":29138,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":262,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2851,"service_tier":"standard"}},"toolName":"Task"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_01T6Gzzz7y8CCKsyb5uDdez1","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update"}}}
./sessions/01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP/events.jsonl:{"ts":1769161525499,"seq":18569,"type":"session.update","session_id":"01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP","data":{"iteration":10,"update":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"toolName":"Task"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_01T6Gzzz7y8CCKsyb5uDdez1","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"## Local Review Report for PR #185\n\nI've completed the local review for PR #185 against the `@daemon-server` spec. Here's the comprehensive analysis:\n\n---\n\n## 1. AC Coverage Analysis - CRITICAL ISSUES FOUND\n\n### Implemented ACs (with test coverage):\n- **ac-1**: Server starts on configurable port ✓ (2 tests)\n- **ac-2**: Binds to localhost only ✓ (1 test)\n- **ac-3**: Rejects non-localhost with 403 ✓ (2 tests)\n- **ac-11**: Health endpoint implementation ✓ (1 test)\n- **ac-12**: Graceful shutdown on SIGTERM/SIGINT ✓ (3 tests)\n- **ac-15**: Plugin pattern for middleware ✓ (2 tests)\n\n### Missing AC Coverage (MUST-FIX):\nThe spec has **16 direct ACs** plus multiple inherited ACs from traits. The PR only covers **6 out of 16 core ACs**. Missing ACs include:\n\n- **ac-4**: File watching with WebSocket broadcast (not implemented)\n- **ac-5**: Debouncing rapid changes (not implemented)\n- **ac-6**: Error handling for YAML parse errors (not implemented)\n- **ac-7**: Recovery with exponential backoff (not implemented)\n- **ac-8**: Fallback to Chokidar (partial - dependency added, not implemented)\n- **ac-9**: Daemon mode with PID file (not implemented)\n- **ac-10**: Stop command (not implemented)\n- **ac-13**: WebSocket ping after 30s inactivity (not implemented)\n- **ac-14**: Close connection after 90s no pong (not implemented)\n- **ac-16**: Bun compile to standalone (not tested)\n\n**Inherited trait ACs** also lack coverage:\n- **@trait-json-output**: 6 ACs (not applicable yet - no JSON mode)\n- **@trait-error-guidance**: 6 ACs (not applicable yet - no error handling)\n- **@trait-shadow-commit**: 8 ACs (not applicable - server doesn't modify shadow)\n- **@trait-localhost-security**: 3 ACs (partially covered by ac-3, but ac-3 from trait mentions warning about external binding config)\n- **@trait-websocket-protocol**: 8 ACs (not implemented)\n\n---\n\n## 2. Test Quality - CRITICAL ISSUES FOUND\n\n### Fluff Tests Identified (MUST-FIX):\n\n**ALL 15 tests in this PR are fluff tests.** They check for implementation details (code structure) rather than actual behavior. Here's the breakdown:\n\n#### Tests that only check for string presence in source code:\n\n1. **Lines 49-60**: Checks `package.json` has Elysia dependency\n   - **Why fluff**: Would pass even if server doesn't work\n   - **Fix needed**: Actually start server, verify it responds on port 3456\n\n2. **Lines 62-72**: Checks index.ts contains `--port=` string\n   - **Why fluff**: Would pass even if flag does nothing\n   - **Fix needed**: Start server with custom port, verify it binds to that port\n\n3. **Lines 74-86**: Checks server.ts contains string 'localhost'\n   - **Why fluff**: String presence doesn't prove binding behavior\n   - **Fix needed**: Try connecting from non-localhost, verify rejection\n\n4. **Lines 88-100**: Checks middleware function name exists\n   - **Why fluff**: Function could exist but not work\n   - **Fix needed**: Make actual HTTP request from non-localhost IP, verify 403\n\n5. **Lines 102-112**: Checks Host header validation code exists\n   - **Why fluff**: Code presence doesn't prove validation works\n   - **Fix needed**: Send requests with different Host headers, verify behavior\n\n6. **Lines 114-127**: Checks health endpoint string exists in source\n   - **Why fluff**: Endpoint could exist but return wrong data\n   - **Fix needed**: Make GET request to /api/health, verify JSON structure\n\n7. **Lines 129-140**: Checks SIGTERM string exists in code\n   - **Why fluff**: Handler could exist but not work\n   - **Fix needed**: Start server, send SIGTERM, verify graceful shutdown\n\n8. **Lines 142-152**: Checks SIGINT string exists in code\n   - **Why fluff**: Same issue as SIGTERM\n   - **Fix needed**: Start server, send SIGINT, verify graceful shutdown\n\n9. **Lines 154-164**: Checks `app.server?.stop()` exists in code\n   - **Why fluff**: Code could exist but fail at runtime\n   - **Fix needed**: Verify server actually stops when signal sent\n\n10. **Lines 166-179**: Checks 'cors' string exists\n    - **Why fluff**: Import doesn't prove CORS works\n    - **Fix needed**: Make CORS preflight request, verify headers\n\n11. **Lines 181-188**: Checks package.json has CORS dependency\n    - **Why fluff**: Dependency presence doesn't prove configuration\n    - **Fix needed**: Actual CORS request verification\n\n12. **Lines 190-197**: Checks chokidar dependency exists\n    - **Why fluff**: Dependency doesn't prove fallback logic\n    - **Fix needed**: Test file watching works or falls back\n\n13. **Lines 199-208**: Checks `.ws(` string exists\n    - **Why fluff**: WebSocket code presence doesn't prove it works\n    - **Fix needed**: Establish WebSocket connection, verify events\n\n14. **Lines 210-219**: Checks `--daemon` string in index.ts\n    - **Why fluff**: Flag presence doesn't prove daemon mode works\n    - **Fix needed**: Start in daemon mode, verify process detaches and PID file created\n\n15. **Lines 221-231**: Checks function signature exists\n    - **Why fluff**: Signature doesn't prove function works\n    - **Fix needed**: Call createServer, verify it returns working server\n\n### Why This is a Problem:\n\n**The litmus test failure**: None of these tests would fail if:\n- Server doesn't start\n- Port binding fails\n- Localhost enforcement breaks\n- Health endpoint returns wrong data\n- Shutdown handlers don't work\n- CORS headers are missing\n\nThese tests verify **\"code exists\"** not **\"feature works\"**.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Test Strategy - NEEDS IMPROVEMENT\n\n### Current Strategy:\n- **0% E2E tests**: No actual server startup or HTTP requests\n- **100% source code inspection**: All tests just read files and check strings\n\n### Recommended Strategy:\n\n**E2E tests should:**\n```typescript\n// GOOD: Test actual behavior\nit('should start server on default port 3456', async () => {\n  // Start actual server\n  const server = spawn('bun', ['run', 'daemon'], { cwd: tempDir });\n  \n  // Wait for server ready\n  await waitForPort(3456);\n  \n  // Make real HTTP request\n  const response = await fetch('http://127.0.0.1:3456/api/health');\n  expect(response.status).toBe(200);\n  \n  const data = await response.json();\n  expect(data).toHaveProperty('status', 'ok');\n  expect(data).toHaveProperty('uptime');\n  \n  // Cleanup\n  server.kill('SIGTERM');\n});\n\n// GOOD: Test rejection behavior\nit('should reject non-localhost with 403', async () => {\n  const server = spawn('bun', ['run', 'daemon'], { cwd: tempDir });\n  await waitForPort(3456);\n  \n  // Send request with non-localhost Host header\n  const response = await fetch('http://127.0.0.1:3456/api/health', {\n    headers: { 'Host': 'evil.com' }\n  });\n  \n  expect(response.status).toBe(403);\n  const data = await response.json();\n  expect(data.error).toBe('Forbidden');\n  \n  server.kill('SIGTERM');\n});\n```\n\n**Unit tests are acceptable for:**\n- Complex validation logic in isolation\n- Helper functions\n- Middleware functions (when tested with mock contexts)\n\nBut for a server implementation, **E2E tests are strongly preferred** because they prove the feature actually works for users.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Test Isolation - PASS\n\n### Analysis:\n✓ All tests use `createTempDir()` in `beforeEach`\n✓ All tests clean up with `cleanupTempDir()` in `afterEach`\n✓ Git repo initialized in temp dir, not kspec repo\n✓ Fixtures copied to temp dir via `setupTempFixtures()`\n\n**However**, the tests don't actually run in temp dirs - they read source files from the project directory:\n```typescript\n// Lines 51-52, 66-67, 77-78, etc.\nawait readFile(join(process.cwd(), 'packages/daemon/...'), 'utf-8')\n```\n\nThis is acceptable for these \"source inspection\" tests, but **real E2E tests MUST run the server from tempDir**:\n```typescript\n// Correct: Run from temp dir\nconst server = spawn('bun', ['run', 'daemon'], { cwd: tempDir });\n\n// Wrong: Run from project dir\nconst server = spawn('bun', ['run', 'daemon']);\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Summary of Blocking Issues\n\n### MUST-FIX (Blocking):\n\n1. **Missing AC Coverage**: Only 6/16 core ACs have any tests at all. The PR claims to implement ac-3 and ac-12, but the spec has 14 other ACs that are completely untested.\n\n2. **All Tests are Fluff**: Every single test just checks if strings exist in source code. None verify actual behavior. Would pass even if server doesn't work.\n\n3. **No E2E Tests**: No actual server startup, no real HTTP requests, no behavior validation.\n\n### Advisory:\n\n4. **Partial Implementation**: The PR correctly implements ac-3 (localhost enforcement) and ac-12 (graceful shutdown), but the scope doesn't match the full spec. This is acceptable IF the task scope was limited to just these ACs.\n\n---\n\n## Recommendations\n\n### Option 1: Fix Tests for Current Scope (Recommended)\nIf the task was only to implement ac-3 and ac-12:\n\n1. **Replace all 15 fluff tests** with 4-5 real E2E tests:\n   - Server starts and responds on default port\n   - Custom port works via --port flag\n   - Non-localhost Host header returns 403\n   - Localhost variations (127.0.0.1, ::1) work\n   - SIGTERM/SIGINT trigger graceful shutdown\n\n2. **Add AC annotations** to match the actual scope:\n   ```typescript\n   // AC: @daemon-server ac-3\n   it('should reject non-localhost with 403', async () => { ... });\n   ```\n\n3. **Run real server** in tests using Bun runtime\n\n### Option 2: Expand Scope to Match Spec\nIf the goal is to complete the full daemon-server spec:\n\n1. Implement missing ACs (ac-4 through ac-14, ac-16)\n2. Write E2E tests for each AC\n3. Add AC annotations for traceability\n\n---\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/tests/daemon-server.test.ts` (233 lines)\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/src/server.ts` (127 lines)\n- Spec: `@daemon-server` (16 core ACs + 31 inherited trait ACs)\n\n---\n\n**Verdict**: **MUST-FIX before merge**. All tests need to be replaced with real E2E tests that verify actual behavior, not source code structure."}},{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"agentId: acaa519 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)"}}]}}}
./sessions/01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP/events.jsonl:{"ts":1769162233164,"seq":19409,"type":"session.update","session_id":"01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP","data":{"iteration":10,"update":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"toolResponse":{"stdout":"OK Started task: 01KFMMM9\n\n--- Spec Context ---\nImplementing: Daemon Server Mode\n\nLong-running Elysia.js server on Bun runtime that exposes kspec state via HTTP API and WebSocket\nfor real-time updates. Binds to localhost only for security. Supports foreground and background\nmodes with PID file management. Includes heartbeat ping/pong for connection health monitoring.\n\n\nAcceptance Criteria (16):\n  [ac-1]\n    Given: kspec is installed\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve'\n    Then: Elysia HTTP server starts on configurable port (default 3456) binding to localhost only\n  [ac-2]\n    Given: daemon is starting\n    When: server binds to network interface\n    Then: only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\n  [ac-3]\n    Given: connection attempt from non-localhost IP\n    When: request received\n    Then: connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\n  [ac-4]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: any .kspec/*.yaml file changes\n    Then: connected WebSocket clients receive update event via topic subscription\n  [ac-5]\n    Given: file watching is active\n    When: rapid changes occur (< 500ms apart)\n    Then: events are debounced and aggregated into single notification\n  [ac-6]\n    Given: watched file has YAML parse error\n    When: change detected\n    Then: error logged and WebSocket broadcasts error event (daemon does not crash)\n  [ac-7]\n    Given: .kspec directory becomes inaccessible\n    When: watcher encounters error\n    Then: daemon logs error and attempts recovery with exponential backoff\n  [ac-8]\n    Given: Bun fs.watch fails or misses events\n    When: reliability issue detected\n    Then: automatically fall back to Chokidar file watcher\n  [ac-9]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve --daemon'\n    Then: process detaches to background, writes PID to .kspec/.daemon.pid, CLI returns immediately\n  [ac-10]\n    Given: daemon is running in background\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve stop'\n    Then: daemon shuts down gracefully, removes PID file, closes all WebSocket connections\n  [ac-11]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: GET /api/health is called\n    Then: returns {status, uptime, connections, version} JSON\n  [ac-12]\n    Given: daemon receives SIGTERM or SIGINT\n    When: shutdown signal received\n    Then: graceful shutdown (flush pending messages, close connections, save state)\n  [ac-13]\n    Given: WebSocket connection established\n    When: 30 seconds pass without activity\n    Then: server sends ping frame\n  [ac-14]\n    Given: ping was sent\n    When: no pong received within 90 seconds\n    Then: connection closed with code 1001\n  [ac-15]\n    Given: Elysia server is configured\n    When: routes are registered\n    Then: use plugin pattern for middleware (CORS, logging, validation)\n  [ac-16]\n    Given: daemon code is ready\n    When: bun build --compile runs\n    Then: produces standalone executable without requiring Bun installation\n\nRemember: Add test coverage for each AC and mark tests with // AC: @spec-ref ac-N","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false},"toolName":"Bash"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_01VmGxeHMEy1KF35EZuBmZHX","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update"}}}
./sessions/01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP/events.jsonl:{"ts":1769162233191,"seq":19410,"type":"session.update","session_id":"01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP","data":{"iteration":10,"update":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"toolName":"Bash"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_01VmGxeHMEy1KF35EZuBmZHX","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"OK Started task: 01KFMMM9\n\n--- Spec Context ---\nImplementing: Daemon Server Mode\n\nLong-running Elysia.js server on Bun runtime that exposes kspec state via HTTP API and WebSocket\nfor real-time updates. Binds to localhost only for security. Supports foreground and background\nmodes with PID file management. Includes heartbeat ping/pong for connection health monitoring.\n\n\nAcceptance Criteria (16):\n  [ac-1]\n    Given: kspec is installed\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve'\n    Then: Elysia HTTP server starts on configurable port (default 3456) binding to localhost only\n  [ac-2]\n    Given: daemon is starting\n    When: server binds to network interface\n    Then: only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\n  [ac-3]\n    Given: connection attempt from non-localhost IP\n    When: request received\n    Then: connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\n  [ac-4]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: any .kspec/*.yaml file changes\n    Then: connected WebSocket clients receive update event via topic subscription\n  [ac-5]\n    Given: file watching is active\n    When: rapid changes occur (< 500ms apart)\n    Then: events are debounced and aggregated into single notification\n  [ac-6]\n    Given: watched file has YAML parse error\n    When: change detected\n    Then: error logged and WebSocket broadcasts error event (daemon does not crash)\n  [ac-7]\n    Given: .kspec directory becomes inaccessible\n    When: watcher encounters error\n    Then: daemon logs error and attempts recovery with exponential backoff\n  [ac-8]\n    Given: Bun fs.watch fails or misses events\n    When: reliability issue detected\n    Then: automatically fall back to Chokidar file watcher\n  [ac-9]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve --daemon'\n    Then: process detaches to background, writes PID to .kspec/.daemon.pid, CLI returns immediately\n  [ac-10]\n    Given: daemon is running in background\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve stop'\n    Then: daemon shuts down gracefully, removes PID file, closes all WebSocket connections\n  [ac-11]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: GET /api/health is called\n    Then: returns {status, uptime, connections, version} JSON\n  [ac-12]\n    Given: daemon receives SIGTERM or SIGINT\n    When: shutdown signal received\n    Then: graceful shutdown (flush pending messages, close connections, save state)\n  [ac-13]\n    Given: WebSocket connection established\n    When: 30 seconds pass without activity\n    Then: server sends ping frame\n  [ac-14]\n    Given: ping was sent\n    When: no pong received within 90 seconds\n    Then: connection closed with code 1001\n  [ac-15]\n    Given: Elysia server is configured\n    When: routes are registered\n    Then: use plugin pattern for middleware (CORS, logging, validation)\n  [ac-16]\n    Given: daemon code is ready\n    When: bun build --compile runs\n    Then: produces standalone executable without requiring Bun installation\n\nRemember: Add test coverage for each AC and mark tests with // AC: @spec-ref ac-N"}}]}}}
./sessions/01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP/events.jsonl:{"ts":1769162540467,"seq":19671,"type":"session.update","session_id":"01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP","data":{"iteration":10,"update":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"toolResponse":{"stdout":"{\n  \"_ulid\": \"01KFHMFGD2563NGHJWPPXGN9CB\",\n  \"slugs\": [\n    \"daemon-server\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"Daemon Server Mode\",\n  \"type\": \"feature\",\n  \"status\": {\n    \"maturity\": \"draft\",\n    \"implementation\": \"in_progress\"\n  },\n  \"tags\": [\n    \"server\",\n    \"websocket\",\n    \"elysia\"\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"Long-running Elysia.js server on Bun runtime that exposes kspec state via HTTP API and WebSocket\\nfor real-time updates. Binds to localhost only for security. Supports foreground and background\\nmodes with PID file management. Includes heartbeat ping/pong for connection health monitoring.\\n\",\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n      \"given\": \"kspec is installed\",\n      \"when\": \"user runs 'kspec serve'\",\n      \"then\": \"Elysia HTTP server starts on configurable port (default 3456) binding to localhost only\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon is starting\",\n      \"when\": \"server binds to network interface\",\n      \"then\": \"only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n      \"given\": \"connection attempt from non-localhost IP\",\n      \"when\": \"request received\",\n      \"then\": \"connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon is running\",\n      \"when\": \"any .kspec/*.yaml file changes\",\n      \"then\": \"connected WebSocket clients receive update event via topic subscription\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n      \"given\": \"file watching is active\",\n      \"when\": \"rapid changes occur (< 500ms apart)\",\n      \"then\": \"events are debounced and aggregated into single notification\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n      \"given\": \"watched file has YAML parse error\",\n      \"when\": \"change detected\",\n      \"then\": \"error logged and WebSocket broadcasts error event (daemon does not crash)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n      \"given\": \".kspec directory becomes inaccessible\",\n      \"when\": \"watcher encounters error\",\n      \"then\": \"daemon logs error and attempts recovery with exponential backoff\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n      \"given\": \"Bun fs.watch fails or misses events\",\n      \"when\": \"reliability issue detected\",\n      \"then\": \"automatically fall back to Chokidar file watcher\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-9\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon is running\",\n      \"when\": \"user runs 'kspec serve --daemon'\",\n      \"then\": \"process detaches to background, writes PID to .kspec/.daemon.pid, CLI returns immediately\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-10\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon is running in background\",\n      \"when\": \"user runs 'kspec serve stop'\",\n      \"then\": \"daemon shuts down gracefully, removes PID file, closes all WebSocket connections\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-11\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon is running\",\n      \"when\": \"GET /api/health is called\",\n      \"then\": \"returns {status, uptime, connections, version} JSON\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-12\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon receives SIGTERM or SIGINT\",\n      \"when\": \"shutdown signal received\",\n      \"then\": \"graceful shutdown (flush pending messages, close connections, save state)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-13\",\n      \"given\": \"WebSocket connection established\",\n      \"when\": \"30 seconds pass without activity\",\n      \"then\": \"server sends ping frame\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-14\",\n      \"given\": \"ping was sent\",\n      \"when\": \"no pong received within 90 seconds\",\n      \"then\": \"connection closed with code 1001\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-15\",\n      \"given\": \"Elysia server is configured\",\n      \"when\": \"routes are registered\",\n      \"then\": \"use plugin pattern for middleware (CORS, logging, validation)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-16\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon code is ready\",\n      \"when\": \"bun build --compile runs\",\n      \"then\": \"produces standalone executable without requiring Bun installation\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"depends_on\": [],\n  \"implements\": [],\n  \"relates_to\": [],\n  \"tests\": [],\n  \"traits\": [\n    \"@trait-json-output\",\n    \"@trait-error-guidance\",\n    \"@trait-shadow-commit\",\n    \"@trait-localhost-security\",\n    \"@trait-websocket-protocol\"\n  ],\n  \"created\": \"2026-01-22T01:18:09.314Z\",\n  \"notes\": [],\n  \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/modules/web-ui.yaml\",\n  \"_path\": \"features[0]\",\n  \"inherited_traits\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-json-output\",\n      \"title\": \"JSON Output Mode\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--json flag is provided\",\n          \"then\": \"output is valid JSON with no ANSI color codes\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command completes successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"output includes all data available in human-readable mode\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command encounters an error\",\n          \"then\": \"error is returned as JSON object with error field\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON output contains references\",\n          \"when\": \"output is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"references use @ prefix consistently\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON output contains timestamps\",\n          \"when\": \"output is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"timestamps use ISO 8601 format\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports --json\",\n          \"when\": \"used with other formatting flags\",\n          \"then\": \"--json takes precedence over other format options\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-error-guidance\",\n      \"title\": \"Error Messages with Recovery Guidance\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters error\",\n          \"when\": \"error message is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"includes description of what went wrong\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters error\",\n          \"when\": \"error message is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"includes suggested action to resolve\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"reference not found\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"suggests checking ref with kspec search or kspec <type> list\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"invalid state transition\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"indicates current state and valid next states\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"validation error\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"indicates which field/value failed validation\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"error in JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--json is active\",\n          \"then\": \"guidance included in structured error object\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-shadow-commit\",\n      \"title\": \"Shadow Branch Auto-Commit\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command modifies state in shadow worktree\",\n          \"when\": \"save operation completes successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"git commit is created in shadow branch with semantic message\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow commit is created\",\n          \"when\": \"commit message is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"message follows pattern operation-colon-ref-short with optional detail\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow commit is created\",\n          \"when\": \"item reference is available\",\n          \"then\": \"commit message includes ULID prefix (8 chars) or primary slug\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow is not configured (no worktree)\",\n          \"when\": \"command that would normally commit runs\",\n          \"then\": \"command completes successfully without attempting git operations\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"save operation fails\",\n          \"when\": \"validation or IO error occurs\",\n          \"then\": \"no commit is attempted and error is returned\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow has remote configured\",\n          \"when\": \"commit succeeds\",\n          \"then\": \"push is attempted in fire-and-forget mode (failure doesn't block command)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n          \"given\": \"commit or push fails\",\n          \"when\": \"save succeeded but git operation failed\",\n          \"then\": \"command succeeds but outputs warning about sync state\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n          \"given\": \"command performs multiple related saves\",\n          \"when\": \"all saves complete successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"single atomic commit covers all changes\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-localhost-security\",\n      \"title\": \"Localhost-Only Security\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"server is starting\",\n          \"when\": \"binding to network interface\",\n          \"then\": \"only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"connection attempt from non-localhost\",\n          \"when\": \"request received\",\n          \"then\": \"connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"server is configured\",\n          \"when\": \"configuration allows external binding\",\n          \"then\": \"warning displayed about security implications\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-websocket-protocol\",\n      \"title\": \"WebSocket Protocol Patterns\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"WebSocket connection is established\",\n          \"when\": \"client connects\",\n          \"then\": \"server assigns unique connection ID and sends connected event with session_id\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"client wants notifications\",\n          \"when\": \"subscribe command sent with topics array\",\n          \"then\": \"server tracks subscription and sends ack with request_id\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"client is subscribed to topic\",\n          \"when\": \"relevant change occurs\",\n          \"then\": \"server broadcasts event with format {msg_id, seq, timestamp, topic, event, data}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"WebSocket connection is active\",\n          \"when\": \"30 seconds pass without activity\",\n          \"then\": \"server sends ping frame\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"ping was sent\",\n          \"when\": \"no pong received within 90 seconds\",\n          \"then\": \"connection is closed with code 1001\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"server sends events\",\n          \"when\": \"client cannot keep up (backpressure)\",\n          \"then\": \"server pauses non-critical broadcasts until drain event\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n          \"given\": \"connection is closing\",\n          \"when\": \"close initiated\",\n          \"then\": \"use code 1000 for clean close, 1001 for timeout, 1011 for error\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n          \"given\": \"client reconnects after disconnect\",\n          \"when\": \"new connection established\",\n          \"then\": \"client resets sequence tracking (lastSeqProcessed = -1) since server generates new sequence\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false},"toolName":"Bash"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_01YBFZim5Z2xMTRREt7rTT2q","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update"}}}
./sessions/01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP/events.jsonl:{"ts":1769162540497,"seq":19672,"type":"session.update","session_id":"01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP","data":{"iteration":10,"update":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"toolName":"Bash"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_01YBFZim5Z2xMTRREt7rTT2q","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"_ulid\": \"01KFHMFGD2563NGHJWPPXGN9CB\",\n  \"slugs\": [\n    \"daemon-server\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"Daemon Server Mode\",\n  \"type\": \"feature\",\n  \"status\": {\n    \"maturity\": \"draft\",\n    \"implementation\": \"in_progress\"\n  },\n  \"tags\": [\n    \"server\",\n    \"websocket\",\n    \"elysia\"\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"Long-running Elysia.js server on Bun runtime that exposes kspec state via HTTP API and WebSocket\\nfor real-time updates. Binds to localhost only for security. Supports foreground and background\\nmodes with PID file management. Includes heartbeat ping/pong for connection health monitoring.\\n\",\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n      \"given\": \"kspec is installed\",\n      \"when\": \"user runs 'kspec serve'\",\n      \"then\": \"Elysia HTTP server starts on configurable port (default 3456) binding to localhost only\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon is starting\",\n      \"when\": \"server binds to network interface\",\n      \"then\": \"only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n      \"given\": \"connection attempt from non-localhost IP\",\n      \"when\": \"request received\",\n      \"then\": \"connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon is running\",\n      \"when\": \"any .kspec/*.yaml file changes\",\n      \"then\": \"connected WebSocket clients receive update event via topic subscription\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n      \"given\": \"file watching is active\",\n      \"when\": \"rapid changes occur (< 500ms apart)\",\n      \"then\": \"events are debounced and aggregated into single notification\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n      \"given\": \"watched file has YAML parse error\",\n      \"when\": \"change detected\",\n      \"then\": \"error logged and WebSocket broadcasts error event (daemon does not crash)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n      \"given\": \".kspec directory becomes inaccessible\",\n      \"when\": \"watcher encounters error\",\n      \"then\": \"daemon logs error and attempts recovery with exponential backoff\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n      \"given\": \"Bun fs.watch fails or misses events\",\n      \"when\": \"reliability issue detected\",\n      \"then\": \"automatically fall back to Chokidar file watcher\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-9\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon is running\",\n      \"when\": \"user runs 'kspec serve --daemon'\",\n      \"then\": \"process detaches to background, writes PID to .kspec/.daemon.pid, CLI returns immediately\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-10\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon is running in background\",\n      \"when\": \"user runs 'kspec serve stop'\",\n      \"then\": \"daemon shuts down gracefully, removes PID file, closes all WebSocket connections\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-11\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon is running\",\n      \"when\": \"GET /api/health is called\",\n      \"then\": \"returns {status, uptime, connections, version} JSON\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-12\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon receives SIGTERM or SIGINT\",\n      \"when\": \"shutdown signal received\",\n      \"then\": \"graceful shutdown (flush pending messages, close connections, save state)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-13\",\n      \"given\": \"WebSocket connection established\",\n      \"when\": \"30 seconds pass without activity\",\n      \"then\": \"server sends ping frame\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-14\",\n      \"given\": \"ping was sent\",\n      \"when\": \"no pong received within 90 seconds\",\n      \"then\": \"connection closed with code 1001\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-15\",\n      \"given\": \"Elysia server is configured\",\n      \"when\": \"routes are registered\",\n      \"then\": \"use plugin pattern for middleware (CORS, logging, validation)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-16\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon code is ready\",\n      \"when\": \"bun build --compile runs\",\n      \"then\": \"produces standalone executable without requiring Bun installation\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"depends_on\": [],\n  \"implements\": [],\n  \"relates_to\": [],\n  \"tests\": [],\n  \"traits\": [\n    \"@trait-json-output\",\n    \"@trait-error-guidance\",\n    \"@trait-shadow-commit\",\n    \"@trait-localhost-security\",\n    \"@trait-websocket-protocol\"\n  ],\n  \"created\": \"2026-01-22T01:18:09.314Z\",\n  \"notes\": [],\n  \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/modules/web-ui.yaml\",\n  \"_path\": \"features[0]\",\n  \"inherited_traits\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-json-output\",\n      \"title\": \"JSON Output Mode\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--json flag is provided\",\n          \"then\": \"output is valid JSON with no ANSI color codes\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command completes successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"output includes all data available in human-readable mode\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command encounters an error\",\n          \"then\": \"error is returned as JSON object with error field\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON output contains references\",\n          \"when\": \"output is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"references use @ prefix consistently\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON output contains timestamps\",\n          \"when\": \"output is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"timestamps use ISO 8601 format\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports --json\",\n          \"when\": \"used with other formatting flags\",\n          \"then\": \"--json takes precedence over other format options\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-error-guidance\",\n      \"title\": \"Error Messages with Recovery Guidance\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters error\",\n          \"when\": \"error message is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"includes description of what went wrong\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters error\",\n          \"when\": \"error message is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"includes suggested action to resolve\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"reference not found\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"suggests checking ref with kspec search or kspec <type> list\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"invalid state transition\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"indicates current state and valid next states\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"validation error\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"indicates which field/value failed validation\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"error in JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--json is active\",\n          \"then\": \"guidance included in structured error object\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-shadow-commit\",\n      \"title\": \"Shadow Branch Auto-Commit\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command modifies state in shadow worktree\",\n          \"when\": \"save operation completes successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"git commit is created in shadow branch with semantic message\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow commit is created\",\n          \"when\": \"commit message is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"message follows pattern operation-colon-ref-short with optional detail\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow commit is created\",\n          \"when\": \"item reference is available\",\n          \"then\": \"commit message includes ULID prefix (8 chars) or primary slug\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow is not configured (no worktree)\",\n          \"when\": \"command that would normally commit runs\",\n          \"then\": \"command completes successfully without attempting git operations\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"save operation fails\",\n          \"when\": \"validation or IO error occurs\",\n          \"then\": \"no commit is attempted and error is returned\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow has remote configured\",\n          \"when\": \"commit succeeds\",\n          \"then\": \"push is attempted in fire-and-forget mode (failure doesn't block command)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n          \"given\": \"commit or push fails\",\n          \"when\": \"save succeeded but git operation failed\",\n          \"then\": \"command succeeds but outputs warning about sync state\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n          \"given\": \"command performs multiple related saves\",\n          \"when\": \"all saves complete successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"single atomic commit covers all changes\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-localhost-security\",\n      \"title\": \"Localhost-Only Security\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"server is starting\",\n          \"when\": \"binding to network interface\",\n          \"then\": \"only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"connection attempt from non-localhost\",\n          \"when\": \"request received\",\n          \"then\": \"connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"server is configured\",\n          \"when\": \"configuration allows external binding\",\n          \"then\": \"warning displayed about security implications\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-websocket-protocol\",\n      \"title\": \"WebSocket Protocol Patterns\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"WebSocket connection is established\",\n          \"when\": \"client connects\",\n          \"then\": \"server assigns unique connection ID and sends connected event with session_id\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"client wants notifications\",\n          \"when\": \"subscribe command sent with topics array\",\n          \"then\": \"server tracks subscription and sends ack with request_id\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"client is subscribed to topic\",\n          \"when\": \"relevant change occurs\",\n          \"then\": \"server broadcasts event with format {msg_id, seq, timestamp, topic, event, data}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"WebSocket connection is active\",\n          \"when\": \"30 seconds pass without activity\",\n          \"then\": \"server sends ping frame\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"ping was sent\",\n          \"when\": \"no pong received within 90 seconds\",\n          \"then\": \"connection is closed with code 1001\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"server sends events\",\n          \"when\": \"client cannot keep up (backpressure)\",\n          \"then\": \"server pauses non-critical broadcasts until drain event\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n          \"given\": \"connection is closing\",\n          \"when\": \"close initiated\",\n          \"then\": \"use code 1000 for clean close, 1001 for timeout, 1011 for error\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n          \"given\": \"client reconnects after disconnect\",\n          \"when\": \"new connection established\",\n          \"then\": \"client resets sequence tracking (lastSeqProcessed = -1) since server generates new sequence\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"}}]}}}
./sessions/01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP/events.jsonl:{"ts":1769162702876,"seq":19921,"type":"session.update","session_id":"01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP","data":{"iteration":10,"update":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"toolResponse":{"stdout":"Daemon Server Mode\n────────────────────────────────────────\nULID:      01KFHMFGD2563NGHJWPPXGN9CB\nSlugs:     daemon-server\nType:      feature\nMaturity:  draft\nImplementation: in_progress\nTags:      server, websocket, elysia\n\n─── Description ───\nLong-running Elysia.js server on Bun runtime that exposes kspec state via HTTP API and WebSocket\nfor real-time updates. Binds to localhost only for security. Supports foreground and background\nmodes with PID file management. Includes heartbeat ping/pong for connection health monitoring.\n\n\n─── Acceptance Criteria ───\n  [ac-1]\n    Given: kspec is installed\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve'\n    Then: Elysia HTTP server starts on configurable port (default 3456) binding to localhost only\n  [ac-2]\n    Given: daemon is starting\n    When: server binds to network interface\n    Then: only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\n  [ac-3]\n    Given: connection attempt from non-localhost IP\n    When: request received\n    Then: connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\n  [ac-4]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: any .kspec/*.yaml file changes\n    Then: connected WebSocket clients receive update event via topic subscription\n  [ac-5]\n    Given: file watching is active\n    When: rapid changes occur (< 500ms apart)\n    Then: events are debounced and aggregated into single notification\n  [ac-6]\n    Given: watched file has YAML parse error\n    When: change detected\n    Then: error logged and WebSocket broadcasts error event (daemon does not crash)\n  [ac-7]\n    Given: .kspec directory becomes inaccessible\n    When: watcher encounters error\n    Then: daemon logs error and attempts recovery with exponential backoff\n  [ac-8]\n    Given: Bun fs.watch fails or misses events\n    When: reliability issue detected\n    Then: automatically fall back to Chokidar file watcher\n  [ac-9]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve --daemon'\n    Then: process detaches to background, writes PID to .kspec/.daemon.pid, CLI returns immediately\n  [ac-10]\n    Given: daemon is running in background\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve stop'\n    Then: daemon shuts down gracefully, removes PID file, closes all WebSocket connections\n  [ac-11]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: GET /api/health is called\n    Then: returns {status, uptime, connections, version} JSON\n  [ac-12]\n    Given: daemon receives SIGTERM or SIGINT\n    When: shutdown signal received\n    Then: graceful shutdown (flush pending messages, close connections, save state)\n  [ac-13]\n    Given: WebSocket connection established\n    When: 30 seconds pass without activity\n    Then: server sends ping frame\n  [ac-14]\n    Given: ping was sent\n    When: no pong received within 90 seconds\n    Then: connection closed with code 1001\n  [ac-15]\n    Given: Elysia server is configured\n    When: routes are registered\n    Then: use plugin pattern for middleware (CORS, logging, validation)\n  [ac-16]\n    Given: daemon code is ready\n    When: bun build --compile runs\n    Then: produces standalone executable without requiring Bun installation\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-json-output ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: command supports JSON mode\n    When: --json flag is provided\n    Then: output is valid JSON with no ANSI color codes\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON mode is active\n    When: command completes successfully\n    Then: output includes all data available in human-readable mode\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON mode is active\n    When: command encounters an error\n    Then: error is returned as JSON object with error field\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON output contains references\n    When: output is generated\n    Then: references use @ prefix consistently\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON output contains timestamps\n    When: output is generated\n    Then: timestamps use ISO 8601 format\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: command supports --json\n    When: used with other formatting flags\n    Then: --json takes precedence over other format options\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-error-guidance ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: command encounters error\n    When: error message is shown\n    Then: includes description of what went wrong\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: command encounters error\n    When: error message is shown\n    Then: includes suggested action to resolve\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: reference not found\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: suggests checking ref with kspec search or kspec <type> list\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: invalid state transition\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: indicates current state and valid next states\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: validation error\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: indicates which field/value failed validation\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: error in JSON mode\n    When: --json is active\n    Then: guidance included in structured error object\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-shadow-commit ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: command modifies state in shadow worktree\n    When: save operation completes successfully\n    Then: git commit is created in shadow branch with semantic message\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow commit is created\n    When: commit message is generated\n    Then: message follows pattern operation-colon-ref-short with optional detail\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow commit is created\n    When: item reference is available\n    Then: commit message includes ULID prefix (8 chars) or primary slug\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow is not configured (no worktree)\n    When: command that would normally commit runs\n    Then: command completes successfully without attempting git operations\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: save operation fails\n    When: validation or IO error occurs\n    Then: no commit is attempted and error is returned\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow has remote configured\n    When: commit succeeds\n    Then: push is attempted in fire-and-forget mode (failure doesn't block command)\n  [ac-7] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: commit or push fails\n    When: save succeeded but git operation failed\n    Then: command succeeds but outputs warning about sync state\n  [ac-8] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: command performs multiple related saves\n    When: all saves complete successfully\n    Then: single atomic commit covers all changes\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-localhost-security ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-localhost-security)\n    Given: server is starting\n    When: binding to network interface\n    Then: only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-localhost-security)\n    Given: connection attempt from non-localhost\n    When: request received\n    Then: connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-localhost-security)\n    Given: server is configured\n    When: configuration allows external binding\n    Then: warning displayed about security implications\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-websocket-protocol ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: WebSocket connection is established\n    When: client connects\n    Then: server assigns unique connection ID and sends connected event with session_id\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: client wants notifications\n    When: subscribe command sent with topics array\n    Then: server tracks subscription and sends ack with request_id\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: client is subscribed to topic\n    When: relevant change occurs\n    Then: server broadcasts event with format {msg_id, seq, timestamp, topic, event, data}\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: WebSocket connection is active\n    When: 30 seconds pass without activity\n    Then: server sends ping frame\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: ping was sent\n    When: no pong received within 90 seconds\n    Then: connection is closed with code 1001\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: server sends events\n    When: client cannot keep up (backpressure)\n    Then: server pauses non-critical broadcasts until drain event\n  [ac-7] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: connection is closing\n    When: close initiated\n    Then: use code 1000 for clean close, 1001 for timeout, 1011 for error\n  [ac-8] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: client reconnects after disconnect\n    When: new connection established\n    Then: client resets sequence tracking (lastSeqProcessed = -1) since server generates new sequence","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false},"toolName":"Bash"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_0133euEzM8iTNQi8j9wagoEU","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update"}}}
