ts\n    When: reliability issue detected\n    Then: automatically fall back to Chokidar file watcher\n  [ac-9]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve --daemon'\n    Then: process detaches to background, writes PID to .kspec/.daemon.pid, CLI returns immediately\n  [ac-10]\n    Given: daemon is running in background\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve stop'\n    Then: daemon shuts down gracefully, removes PID file, closes all WebSocket connections\n  [ac-11]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: GET /api/health is called\n    Then: returns {status, uptime, connections, version} JSON\n  [ac-12]\n    Given: daemon receives SIGTERM or SIGINT\n    When: shutdown signal received\n    Then: graceful shutdown (flush pending messages, close connections, save state)\n  [ac-13]\n    Given: WebSocket connection established\n    When: 30 seconds pass without activity\n    Then: server sends ping frame\n  [ac-14]\n    Given: ping was sent\n    When: no pong received within 90 seconds\n    Then: connection closed with code 1001\n  [ac-15]\n    Given: Elysia server is configured\n    When: routes are registered\n    Then: use plugin pattern for middleware (CORS, logging, validation)\n  [ac-16]\n    Given: daemon code is ready\n    When: bun build --compile runs\n    Then: produces standalone executable without requiring Bun installation\n\nRemember: Add test coverage for each AC and mark tests with // AC: @spec-ref ac-N"}}]}}}
./sessions/01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP/events.jsonl:{"ts":1769165013851,"seq":22854,"type":"session.update","session_id":"01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP","data":{"iteration":10,"update":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"toolResponse":{"stdout":"{\n  \"_ulid\": \"01KFHMFGD2563NGHJWPPXGN9CB\",\n  \"slugs\": [\n    \"daemon-server\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"Daemon Server Mode\",\n  \"type\": \"feature\",\n  \"status\": {\n    \"maturity\": \"draft\",\n    \"implementation\": \"in_progress\"\n  },\n  \"tags\": [\n    \"server\",\n    \"websocket\",\n    \"elysia\"\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"Long-running Elysia.js server on Bun runtime that exposes kspec state via HTTP API and WebSocket\\nfor real-time updates. Binds to localhost only for security. Supports foreground and background\\nmodes with PID file management. Includes heartbeat ping/pong for connection health monitoring.\\n\",\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n      \"given\": \"kspec is installed\",\n      \"when\": \"user runs 'kspec serve'\",\n      \"then\": \"Elysia HTTP server starts on configurable port (default 3456) binding to localhost only\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon is starting\",\n      \"when\": \"server binds to network interface\",\n      \"then\": \"only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n      \"given\": \"connection attempt from non-localhost IP\",\n      \"when\": \"request received\",\n      \"then\": \"connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon is running\",\n      \"when\": \"any .kspec/*.yaml file changes\",\n      \"then\": \"connected WebSocket clients receive update event via topic subscription\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n      \"given\": \"file watching is active\",\n      \"when\": \"rapid changes occur (< 500ms apart)\",\n      \"then\": \"events are debounced and aggregated into single notification\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n      \"given\": \"watched file has YAML parse error\",\n      \"when\": \"change detected\",\n      \"then\": \"error logged and WebSocket broadcasts error event (daemon does not crash)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n      \"given\": \".kspec directory becomes inaccessible\",\n      \"when\": \"watcher encounters error\",\n      \"then\": \"daemon logs error and attempts recovery with exponential backoff\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n      \"given\": \"Bun fs.watch fails or misses events\",\n      \"when\": \"reliability issue detected\",\n      \"then\": \"automatically fall back to Chokidar file watcher\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-9\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon is running\",\n      \"when\": \"user runs 'kspec serve --daemon'\",\n      \"then\": \"process detaches to background, writes PID to .kspec/.daemon.pid, CLI returns immediately\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-10\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon is running in background\",\n      \"when\": \"user runs 'kspec serve stop'\",\n      \"then\": \"daemon shuts down gracefully, removes PID file, closes all WebSocket connections\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-11\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon is running\",\n      \"when\": \"GET /api/health is called\",\n      \"then\": \"returns {status, uptime, connections, version} JSON\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-12\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon receives SIGTERM or SIGINT\",\n      \"when\": \"shutdown signal received\",\n      \"then\": \"graceful shutdown (flush pending messages, close connections, save state)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-13\",\n      \"given\": \"WebSocket connection established\",\n      \"when\": \"30 seconds pass without activity\",\n      \"then\": \"server sends ping frame\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-14\",\n      \"given\": \"ping was sent\",\n      \"when\": \"no pong received within 90 seconds\",\n      \"then\": \"connection closed with code 1001\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-15\",\n      \"given\": \"Elysia server is configured\",\n      \"when\": \"routes are registered\",\n      \"then\": \"use plugin pattern for middleware (CORS, logging, validation)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-16\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon code is ready\",\n      \"when\": \"bun build --compile runs\",\n      \"then\": \"produces standalone executable without requiring Bun installation\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"depends_on\": [],\n  \"implements\": [],\n  \"relates_to\": [],\n  \"tests\": [],\n  \"traits\": [\n    \"@trait-json-output\",\n    \"@trait-error-guidance\",\n    \"@trait-shadow-commit\",\n    \"@trait-localhost-security\",\n    \"@trait-websocket-protocol\"\n  ],\n  \"created\": \"2026-01-22T01:18:09.314Z\",\n  \"notes\": [],\n  \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/modules/web-ui.yaml\",\n  \"_path\": \"features[0]\",\n  \"inherited_traits\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-json-output\",\n      \"title\": \"JSON Output Mode\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--json flag is provided\",\n          \"then\": \"output is valid JSON with no ANSI color codes\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command completes successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"output includes all data available in human-readable mode\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command encounters an error\",\n          \"then\": \"error is returned as JSON object with error field\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON output contains references\",\n          \"when\": \"output is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"references use @ prefix consistently\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON output contains timestamps\",\n          \"when\": \"output is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"timestamps use ISO 8601 format\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports --json\",\n          \"when\": \"used with other formatting flags\",\n          \"then\": \"--json takes precedence over other format options\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-error-guidance\",\n      \"title\": \"Error Messages with Recovery Guidance\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters error\",\n          \"when\": \"error message is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"includes description of what went wrong\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters error\",\n          \"when\": \"error message is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"includes suggested action to resolve\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"reference not found\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"suggests checking ref with kspec search or kspec <type> list\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"invalid state transition\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"indicates current state and valid next states\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"validation error\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"indicates which field/value failed validation\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"error in JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--json is active\",\n          \"then\": \"guidance included in structured error object\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-shadow-commit\",\n      \"title\": \"Shadow Branch Auto-Commit\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command modifies state in shadow worktree\",\n          \"when\": \"save operation completes successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"git commit is created in shadow branch with semantic message\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow commit is created\",\n          \"when\": \"commit message is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"message follows pattern operation-colon-ref-short with optional detail\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow commit is created\",\n          \"when\": \"item reference is available\",\n          \"then\": \"commit message includes ULID prefix (8 chars) or primary slug\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow is not configured (no worktree)\",\n          \"when\": \"command that would normally commit runs\",\n          \"then\": \"command completes successfully without attempting git operations\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"save operation fails\",\n          \"when\": \"validation or IO error occurs\",\n          \"then\": \"no commit is attempted and error is returned\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow has remote configured\",\n          \"when\": \"commit succeeds\",\n          \"then\": \"push is attempted in fire-and-forget mode (failure doesn't block command)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n          \"given\": \"commit or push fails\",\n          \"when\": \"save succeeded but git operation failed\",\n          \"then\": \"command succeeds but outputs warning about sync state\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n          \"given\": \"command performs multiple related saves\",\n          \"when\": \"all saves complete successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"single atomic commit covers all changes\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-localhost-security\",\n      \"title\": \"Localhost-Only Security\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"server is starting\",\n          \"when\": \"binding to network interface\",\n          \"then\": \"only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"connection attempt from non-localhost\",\n          \"when\": \"request received\",\n          \"then\": \"connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"server is configured\",\n          \"when\": \"configuration allows external binding\",\n          \"then\": \"warning displayed about security implications\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-websocket-protocol\",\n      \"title\": \"WebSocket Protocol Patterns\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"WebSocket connection is established\",\n          \"when\": \"client connects\",\n          \"then\": \"server assigns unique connection ID and sends connected event with session_id\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"client wants notifications\",\n          \"when\": \"subscribe command sent with topics array\",\n          \"then\": \"server tracks subscription and sends ack with request_id\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"client is subscribed to topic\",\n          \"when\": \"relevant change occurs\",\n          \"then\": \"server broadcasts event with format {msg_id, seq, timestamp, topic, event, data}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"WebSocket connection is active\",\n          \"when\": \"30 seconds pass without activity\",\n          \"then\": \"server sends ping frame\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"ping was sent\",\n          \"when\": \"no pong received within 90 seconds\",\n          \"then\": \"connection is closed with code 1001\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"server sends events\",\n          \"when\": \"client cannot keep up (backpressure)\",\n          \"then\": \"server pauses non-critical broadcasts until drain event\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n          \"given\": \"connection is closing\",\n          \"when\": \"close initiated\",\n          \"then\": \"use code 1000 for clean close, 1001 for timeout, 1011 for error\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n          \"given\": \"client reconnects after disconnect\",\n          \"when\": \"new connection established\",\n          \"then\": \"client resets sequence tracking (lastSeqProcessed = -1) since server generates new sequence\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false},"toolName":"Bash"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_01DMAcTzQpQ7iiXCCUkb6o8G","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update"}}}
./sessions/01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP/events.jsonl:{"ts":1769165013880,"seq":22855,"type":"session.update","session_id":"01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP","data":{"iteration":10,"update":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"toolName":"Bash"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_01DMAcTzQpQ7iiXCCUkb6o8G","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"_ulid\": \"01KFHMFGD2563NGHJWPPXGN9CB\",\n  \"slugs\": [\n    \"daemon-server\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"Daemon Server Mode\",\n  \"type\": \"feature\",\n  \"status\": {\n    \"maturity\": \"draft\",\n    \"implementation\": \"in_progress\"\n  },\n  \"tags\": [\n    \"server\",\n    \"websocket\",\n    \"elysia\"\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"Long-running Elysia.js server on Bun runtime that exposes kspec state via HTTP API and WebSocket\\nfor real-time updates. Binds to localhost only for security. Supports foreground and background\\nmodes with PID file management. Includes heartbeat ping/pong for connection health monitoring.\\n\",\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n      \"given\": \"kspec is installed\",\n      \"when\": \"user runs 'kspec serve'\",\n      \"then\": \"Elysia HTTP server starts on configurable port (default 3456) binding to localhost only\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon is starting\",\n      \"when\": \"server binds to network interface\",\n      \"then\": \"only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n      \"given\": \"connection attempt from non-localhost IP\",\n      \"when\": \"request received\",\n      \"then\": \"connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon is running\",\n      \"when\": \"any .kspec/*.yaml file changes\",\n      \"then\": \"connected WebSocket clients receive update event via topic subscription\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n      \"given\": \"file watching is active\",\n      \"when\": \"rapid changes occur (< 500ms apart)\",\n      \"then\": \"events are debounced and aggregated into single notification\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n      \"given\": \"watched file has YAML parse error\",\n      \"when\": \"change detected\",\n      \"then\": \"error logged and WebSocket broadcasts error event (daemon does not crash)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n      \"given\": \".kspec directory becomes inaccessible\",\n      \"when\": \"watcher encounters error\",\n      \"then\": \"daemon logs error and attempts recovery with exponential backoff\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n      \"given\": \"Bun fs.watch fails or misses events\",\n      \"when\": \"reliability issue detected\",\n      \"then\": \"automatically fall back to Chokidar file watcher\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-9\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon is running\",\n      \"when\": \"user runs 'kspec serve --daemon'\",\n      \"then\": \"process detaches to background, writes PID to .kspec/.daemon.pid, CLI returns immediately\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-10\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon is running in background\",\n      \"when\": \"user runs 'kspec serve stop'\",\n      \"then\": \"daemon shuts down gracefully, removes PID file, closes all WebSocket connections\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-11\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon is running\",\n      \"when\": \"GET /api/health is called\",\n      \"then\": \"returns {status, uptime, connections, version} JSON\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-12\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon receives SIGTERM or SIGINT\",\n      \"when\": \"shutdown signal received\",\n      \"then\": \"graceful shutdown (flush pending messages, close connections, save state)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-13\",\n      \"given\": \"WebSocket connection established\",\n      \"when\": \"30 seconds pass without activity\",\n      \"then\": \"server sends ping frame\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-14\",\n      \"given\": \"ping was sent\",\n      \"when\": \"no pong received within 90 seconds\",\n      \"then\": \"connection closed with code 1001\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-15\",\n      \"given\": \"Elysia server is configured\",\n      \"when\": \"routes are registered\",\n      \"then\": \"use plugin pattern for middleware (CORS, logging, validation)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ac-16\",\n      \"given\": \"daemon code is ready\",\n      \"when\": \"bun build --compile runs\",\n      \"then\": \"produces standalone executable without requiring Bun installation\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"depends_on\": [],\n  \"implements\": [],\n  \"relates_to\": [],\n  \"tests\": [],\n  \"traits\": [\n    \"@trait-json-output\",\n    \"@trait-error-guidance\",\n    \"@trait-shadow-commit\",\n    \"@trait-localhost-security\",\n    \"@trait-websocket-protocol\"\n  ],\n  \"created\": \"2026-01-22T01:18:09.314Z\",\n  \"notes\": [],\n  \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/modules/web-ui.yaml\",\n  \"_path\": \"features[0]\",\n  \"inherited_traits\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-json-output\",\n      \"title\": \"JSON Output Mode\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--json flag is provided\",\n          \"then\": \"output is valid JSON with no ANSI color codes\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command completes successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"output includes all data available in human-readable mode\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command encounters an error\",\n          \"then\": \"error is returned as JSON object with error field\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON output contains references\",\n          \"when\": \"output is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"references use @ prefix consistently\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON output contains timestamps\",\n          \"when\": \"output is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"timestamps use ISO 8601 format\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports --json\",\n          \"when\": \"used with other formatting flags\",\n          \"then\": \"--json takes precedence over other format options\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-error-guidance\",\n      \"title\": \"Error Messages with Recovery Guidance\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters error\",\n          \"when\": \"error message is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"includes description of what went wrong\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters error\",\n          \"when\": \"error message is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"includes suggested action to resolve\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"reference not found\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"suggests checking ref with kspec search or kspec <type> list\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"invalid state transition\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"indicates current state and valid next states\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"validation error\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"indicates which field/value failed validation\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"error in JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--json is active\",\n          \"then\": \"guidance included in structured error object\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-shadow-commit\",\n      \"title\": \"Shadow Branch Auto-Commit\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command modifies state in shadow worktree\",\n          \"when\": \"save operation completes successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"git commit is created in shadow branch with semantic message\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow commit is created\",\n          \"when\": \"commit message is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"message follows pattern operation-colon-ref-short with optional detail\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow commit is created\",\n          \"when\": \"item reference is available\",\n          \"then\": \"commit message includes ULID prefix (8 chars) or primary slug\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow is not configured (no worktree)\",\n          \"when\": \"command that would normally commit runs\",\n          \"then\": \"command completes successfully without attempting git operations\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"save operation fails\",\n          \"when\": \"validation or IO error occurs\",\n          \"then\": \"no commit is attempted and error is returned\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow has remote configured\",\n          \"when\": \"commit succeeds\",\n          \"then\": \"push is attempted in fire-and-forget mode (failure doesn't block command)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n          \"given\": \"commit or push fails\",\n          \"when\": \"save succeeded but git operation failed\",\n          \"then\": \"command succeeds but outputs warning about sync state\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n          \"given\": \"command performs multiple related saves\",\n          \"when\": \"all saves complete successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"single atomic commit covers all changes\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-localhost-security\",\n      \"title\": \"Localhost-Only Security\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"server is starting\",\n          \"when\": \"binding to network interface\",\n          \"then\": \"only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"connection attempt from non-localhost\",\n          \"when\": \"request received\",\n          \"then\": \"connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"server is configured\",\n          \"when\": \"configuration allows external binding\",\n          \"then\": \"warning displayed about security implications\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-websocket-protocol\",\n      \"title\": \"WebSocket Protocol Patterns\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"WebSocket connection is established\",\n          \"when\": \"client connects\",\n          \"then\": \"server assigns unique connection ID and sends connected event with session_id\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"client wants notifications\",\n          \"when\": \"subscribe command sent with topics array\",\n          \"then\": \"server tracks subscription and sends ack with request_id\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"client is subscribed to topic\",\n          \"when\": \"relevant change occurs\",\n          \"then\": \"server broadcasts event with format {msg_id, seq, timestamp, topic, event, data}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"WebSocket connection is active\",\n          \"when\": \"30 seconds pass without activity\",\n          \"then\": \"server sends ping frame\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"ping was sent\",\n          \"when\": \"no pong received within 90 seconds\",\n          \"then\": \"connection is closed with code 1001\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"server sends events\",\n          \"when\": \"client cannot keep up (backpressure)\",\n          \"then\": \"server pauses non-critical broadcasts until drain event\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n          \"given\": \"connection is closing\",\n          \"when\": \"close initiated\",\n          \"then\": \"use code 1000 for clean close, 1001 for timeout, 1011 for error\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n          \"given\": \"client reconnects after disconnect\",\n          \"when\": \"new connection established\",\n          \"then\": \"client resets sequence tracking (lastSeqProcessed = -1) since server generates new sequence\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"}}]}}}
./sessions/01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP/events.jsonl:{"ts":1769165189880,"seq":23161,"type":"session.update","session_id":"01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP","data":{"iteration":10,"update":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"toolResponse":{"stdout":"Daemon Server Mode\n────────────────────────────────────────\nULID:      01KFHMFGD2563NGHJWPPXGN9CB\nSlugs:     daemon-server\nType:      feature\nMaturity:  draft\nImplementation: in_progress\nTags:      server, websocket, elysia\n\n─── Description ───\nLong-running Elysia.js server on Bun runtime that exposes kspec state via HTTP API and WebSocket\nfor real-time updates. Binds to localhost only for security. Supports foreground and background\nmodes with PID file management. Includes heartbeat ping/pong for connection health monitoring.\n\n\n─── Acceptance Criteria ───\n  [ac-1]\n    Given: kspec is installed\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve'\n    Then: Elysia HTTP server starts on configurable port (default 3456) binding to localhost only\n  [ac-2]\n    Given: daemon is starting\n    When: server binds to network interface\n    Then: only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\n  [ac-3]\n    Given: connection attempt from non-localhost IP\n    When: request received\n    Then: connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\n  [ac-4]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: any .kspec/*.yaml file changes\n    Then: connected WebSocket clients receive update event via topic subscription\n  [ac-5]\n    Given: file watching is active\n    When: rapid changes occur (< 500ms apart)\n    Then: events are debounced and aggregated into single notification\n  [ac-6]\n    Given: watched file has YAML parse error\n    When: change detected\n    Then: error logged and WebSocket broadcasts error event (daemon does not crash)\n  [ac-7]\n    Given: .kspec directory becomes inaccessible\n    When: watcher encounters error\n    Then: daemon logs error and attempts recovery with exponential backoff\n  [ac-8]\n    Given: Bun fs.watch fails or misses events\n    When: reliability issue detected\n    Then: automatically fall back to Chokidar file watcher\n  [ac-9]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve --daemon'\n    Then: process detaches to background, writes PID to .kspec/.daemon.pid, CLI returns immediately\n  [ac-10]\n    Given: daemon is running in background\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve stop'\n    Then: daemon shuts down gracefully, removes PID file, closes all WebSocket connections\n  [ac-11]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: GET /api/health is called\n    Then: returns {status, uptime, connections, version} JSON\n  [ac-12]\n    Given: daemon receives SIGTERM or SIGINT\n    When: shutdown signal received\n    Then: graceful shutdown (flush pending messages, close connections, save state)\n  [ac-13]\n    Given: WebSocket connection established\n    When: 30 seconds pass without activity\n    Then: server sends ping frame\n  [ac-14]\n    Given: ping was sent\n    When: no pong received within 90 seconds\n    Then: connection closed with code 1001\n  [ac-15]\n    Given: Elysia server is configured\n    When: routes are registered\n    Then: use plugin pattern for middleware (CORS, logging, validation)\n  [ac-16]\n    Given: daemon code is ready\n    When: bun build --compile runs\n    Then: produces standalone executable without requiring Bun installation\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-json-output ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: command supports JSON mode\n    When: --json flag is provided\n    Then: output is valid JSON with no ANSI color codes\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON mode is active\n    When: command completes successfully\n    Then: output includes all data available in human-readable mode\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON mode is active\n    When: command encounters an error\n    Then: error is returned as JSON object with error field\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON output contains references\n    When: output is generated\n    Then: references use @ prefix consistently\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON output contains timestamps\n    When: output is generated\n    Then: timestamps use ISO 8601 format\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: command supports --json\n    When: used with other formatting flags\n    Then: --json takes precedence over other format options\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-error-guidance ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: command encounters error\n    When: error message is shown\n    Then: includes description of what went wrong\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: command encounters error\n    When: error message is shown\n    Then: includes suggested action to resolve\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: reference not found\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: suggests checking ref with kspec search or kspec <type> list\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: invalid state transition\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: indicates current state and valid next states\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: validation error\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: indicates which field/value failed validation\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: error in JSON mode\n    When: --json is active\n    Then: guidance included in structured error object\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-shadow-commit ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: command modifies state in shadow worktree\n    When: save operation completes successfully\n    Then: git commit is created in shadow branch with semantic message\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow commit is created\n    When: commit message is generated\n    Then: message follows pattern operation-colon-ref-short with optional detail\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow commit is created\n    When: item reference is available\n    Then: commit message includes ULID prefix (8 chars) or primary slug\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow is not configured (no worktree)\n    When: command that would normally commit runs\n    Then: command completes successfully without attempting git operations\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: save operation fails\n    When: validation or IO error occurs\n    Then: no commit is attempted and error is returned\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow has remote configured\n    When: commit succeeds\n    Then: push is attempted in fire-and-forget mode (failure doesn't block command)\n  [ac-7] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: commit or push fails\n    When: save succeeded but git operation failed\n    Then: command succeeds but outputs warning about sync state\n  [ac-8] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: command performs multiple related saves\n    When: all saves complete successfully\n    Then: single atomic commit covers all changes\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-localhost-security ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-localhost-security)\n    Given: server is starting\n    When: binding to network interface\n    Then: only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-localhost-security)\n    Given: connection attempt from non-localhost\n    When: request received\n    Then: connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-localhost-security)\n    Given: server is configured\n    When: configuration allows external binding\n    Then: warning displayed about security implications\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-websocket-protocol ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: WebSocket connection is established\n    When: client connects\n    Then: server assigns unique connection ID and sends connected event with session_id\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: client wants notifications\n    When: subscribe command sent with topics array\n    Then: server tracks subscription and sends ack with request_id\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: client is subscribed to topic\n    When: relevant change occurs\n    Then: server broadcasts event with format {msg_id, seq, timestamp, topic, event, data}\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: WebSocket connection is active\n    When: 30 seconds pass without activity\n    Then: server sends ping frame\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: ping was sent\n    When: no pong received within 90 seconds\n    Then: connection is closed with code 1001\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: server sends events\n    When: client cannot keep up (backpressure)\n    Then: server pauses non-critical broadcasts until drain event\n  [ac-7] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: connection is closing\n    When: close initiated\n    Then: use code 1000 for clean close, 1001 for timeout, 1011 for error\n  [ac-8] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: client reconnects after disconnect\n    When: new connection established\n    Then: client resets sequence tracking (lastSeqProcessed = -1) since server generates new sequence","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false},"toolName":"Bash"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_01FujsZEJbzvrvCrB6zGfonN","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update"}}}
./sessions/01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP/events.jsonl:{"ts":1769165189910,"seq":23162,"type":"session.update","session_id":"01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP","data":{"iteration":10,"update":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"toolName":"Bash"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_01FujsZEJbzvrvCrB6zGfonN","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"Daemon Server Mode\n────────────────────────────────────────\nULID:      01KFHMFGD2563NGHJWPPXGN9CB\nSlugs:     daemon-server\nType:      feature\nMaturity:  draft\nImplementation: in_progress\nTags:      server, websocket, elysia\n\n─── Description ───\nLong-running Elysia.js server on Bun runtime that exposes kspec state via HTTP API and WebSocket\nfor real-time updates. Binds to localhost only for security. Supports foreground and background\nmodes with PID file management. Includes heartbeat ping/pong for connection health monitoring.\n\n\n─── Acceptance Criteria ───\n  [ac-1]\n    Given: kspec is installed\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve'\n    Then: Elysia HTTP server starts on configurable port (default 3456) binding to localhost only\n  [ac-2]\n    Given: daemon is starting\n    When: server binds to network interface\n    Then: only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\n  [ac-3]\n    Given: connection attempt from non-localhost IP\n    When: request received\n    Then: connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\n  [ac-4]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: any .kspec/*.yaml file changes\n    Then: connected WebSocket clients receive update event via topic subscription\n  [ac-5]\n    Given: file watching is active\n    When: rapid changes occur (< 500ms apart)\n    Then: events are debounced and aggregated into single notification\n  [ac-6]\n    Given: watched file has YAML parse error\n    When: change detected\n    Then: error logged and WebSocket broadcasts error event (daemon does not crash)\n  [ac-7]\n    Given: .kspec directory becomes inaccessible\n    When: watcher encounters error\n    Then: daemon logs error and attempts recovery with exponential backoff\n  [ac-8]\n    Given: Bun fs.watch fails or misses events\n    When: reliability issue detected\n    Then: automatically fall back to Chokidar file watcher\n  [ac-9]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve --daemon'\n    Then: process detaches to background, writes PID to .kspec/.daemon.pid, CLI returns immediately\n  [ac-10]\n    Given: daemon is running in background\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve stop'\n    Then: daemon shuts down gracefully, removes PID file, closes all WebSocket connections\n  [ac-11]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: GET /api/health is called\n    Then: returns {status, uptime, connections, version} JSON\n  [ac-12]\n    Given: daemon receives SIGTERM or SIGINT\n    When: shutdown signal received\n    Then: graceful shutdown (flush pending messages, close connections, save state)\n  [ac-13]\n    Given: WebSocket connection established\n    When: 30 seconds pass without activity\n    Then: server sends ping frame\n  [ac-14]\n    Given: ping was sent\n    When: no pong received within 90 seconds\n    Then: connection closed with code 1001\n  [ac-15]\n    Given: Elysia server is configured\n    When: routes are registered\n    Then: use plugin pattern for middleware (CORS, logging, validation)\n  [ac-16]\n    Given: daemon code is ready\n    When: bun build --compile runs\n    Then: produces standalone executable without requiring Bun installation\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-json-output ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: command supports JSON mode\n    When: --json flag is provided\n    Then: output is valid JSON with no ANSI color codes\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON mode is active\n    When: command completes successfully\n    Then: output includes all data available in human-readable mode\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON mode is active\n    When: command encounters an error\n    Then: error is returned as JSON object with error field\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON output contains references\n    When: output is generated\n    Then: references use @ prefix consistently\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON output contains timestamps\n    When: output is generated\n    Then: timestamps use ISO 8601 format\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: command supports --json\n    When: used with other formatting flags\n    Then: --json takes precedence over other format options\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-error-guidance ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: command encounters error\n    When: error message is shown\n    Then: includes description of what went wrong\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: command encounters error\n    When: error message is shown\n    Then: includes suggested action to resolve\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: reference not found\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: suggests checking ref with kspec search or kspec <type> list\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: invalid state transition\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: indicates current state and valid next states\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: validation error\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: indicates which field/value failed validation\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: error in JSON mode\n    When: --json is active\n    Then: guidance included in structured error object\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-shadow-commit ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: command modifies state in shadow worktree\n    When: save operation completes successfully\n    Then: git commit is created in shadow branch with semantic message\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow commit is created\n    When: commit message is generated\n    Then: message follows pattern operation-colon-ref-short with optional detail\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow commit is created\n    When: item reference is available\n    Then: commit message includes ULID prefix (8 chars) or primary slug\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow is not configured (no worktree)\n    When: command that would normally commit runs\n    Then: command completes successfully without attempting git operations\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: save operation fails\n    When: validation or IO error occurs\n    Then: no commit is attempted and error is returned\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow has remote configured\n    When: commit succeeds\n    Then: push is attempted in fire-and-forget mode (failure doesn't block command)\n  [ac-7] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: commit or push fails\n    When: save succeeded but git operation failed\n    Then: command succeeds but outputs warning about sync state\n  [ac-8] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: command performs multiple related saves\n    When: all saves complete successfully\n    Then: single atomic commit covers all changes\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-localhost-security ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-localhost-security)\n    Given: server is starting\n    When: binding to network interface\n    Then: only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-localhost-security)\n    Given: connection attempt from non-localhost\n    When: request received\n    Then: connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-localhost-security)\n    Given: server is configured\n    When: configuration allows external binding\n    Then: warning displayed about security implications\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-websocket-protocol ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: WebSocket connection is established\n    When: client connects\n    Then: server assigns unique connection ID and sends connected event with session_id\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: client wants notifications\n    When: subscribe command sent with topics array\n    Then: server tracks subscription and sends ack with request_id\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: client is subscribed to topic\n    When: relevant change occurs\n    Then: server broadcasts event with format {msg_id, seq, timestamp, topic, event, data}\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: WebSocket connection is active\n    When: 30 seconds pass without activity\n    Then: server sends ping frame\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: ping was sent\n    When: no pong received within 90 seconds\n    Then: connection is closed with code 1001\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: server sends events\n    When: client cannot keep up (backpressure)\n    Then: server pauses non-critical broadcasts until drain event\n  [ac-7] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: connection is closing\n    When: close initiated\n    Then: use code 1000 for clean close, 1001 for timeout, 1011 for error\n  [ac-8] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: client reconnects after disconnect\n    When: new connection established\n    Then: client resets sequence tracking (lastSeqProcessed = -1) since server generates new sequence"}}]}}}
./sessions/01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP/events.jsonl:{"ts":1769165246295,"seq":23203,"type":"session.update","session_id":"01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP","data":{"iteration":10,"update":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"toolResponse":{"stdout":"Implement daemon process detach\n────────────────────────────────────────\nULID:      01KFMMMH7B711BQZ8WFT4PVQT4\nType:      task\nStatus:    pending_review\nPriority:  2\nAutomation: eligible\nSpec ref:  @daemon-server\nTags:      phase-1, daemon\nCreated:   2026-01-23T05:18:37.290Z\nStarted:   2026-01-23T10:38:36.162Z\n\n─── Spec Context ───\nDaemon Server Mode\nType: feature\nImplementation: in_progress\nDescription:\n  Long-running Elysia.js server on Bun runtime that exposes kspec state via HTTP API and WebSocket\n  for real-time updates. Binds to localhost only for security. Supports foreground and background\n  modes with PID file management. Includes heartbeat ping/pong for connection health monitoring.\nAcceptance Criteria:\n  [ac-1]\n    Given: kspec is installed\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve'\n    Then: Elysia HTTP server starts on configurable port (default 3456) binding to localhost only\n  [ac-2]\n    Given: daemon is starting\n    When: server binds to network interface\n    Then: only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\n  [ac-3]\n    Given: connection attempt from non-localhost IP\n    When: request received\n    Then: connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\n  [ac-4]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: any .kspec/*.yaml file changes\n    Then: connected WebSocket clients receive update event via topic subscription\n  [ac-5]\n    Given: file watching is active\n    When: rapid changes occur (< 500ms apart)\n    Then: events are debounced and aggregated into single notification\n  [ac-6]\n    Given: watched file has YAML parse error\n    When: change detected\n    Then: error logged and WebSocket broadcasts error event (daemon does not crash)\n  [ac-7]\n    Given: .kspec directory becomes inaccessible\n    When: watcher encounters error\n    Then: daemon logs error and attempts recovery with exponential backoff\n  [ac-8]\n    Given: Bun fs.watch fails or misses events\n    When: reliability issue detected\n    Then: automatically fall back to Chokidar file watcher\n  [ac-9]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve --daemon'\n    Then: process detaches to background, writes PID to .kspec/.daemon.pid, CLI returns immediately\n  [ac-10]\n    Given: daemon is running in background\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve stop'\n    Then: daemon shuts down gracefully, removes PID file, closes all WebSocket connections\n  [ac-11]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: GET /api/health is called\n    Then: returns {status, uptime, connections, version} JSON\n  [ac-12]\n    Given: daemon receives SIGTERM or SIGINT\n    When: shutdown signal received\n    Then: graceful shutdown (flush pending messages, close connections, save state)\n  [ac-13]\n    Given: WebSocket connection established\n    When: 30 seconds pass without activity\n    Then: server sends ping frame\n  [ac-14]\n    Given: ping was sent\n    When: no pong received within 90 seconds\n    Then: connection closed with code 1001\n  [ac-15]\n    Given: Elysia server is configured\n    When: routes are registered\n    Then: use plugin pattern for middleware (CORS, logging, validation)\n  [ac-16]\n    Given: daemon code is ready\n    When: bun build --compile runs\n    Then: produces standalone executable without requiring Bun installation\n\n─── Notes ───\n[2026-01-23T05:19:36.801Z] @claude:\n## Implementation Notes\n\n### Objective\nImplement daemon background mode with process detach, PID file management.\n\n### Steps\n1. Implement --daemon flag handling:\n   ```typescript\n   if (args.daemon) {\n     const child = Bun.spawn(['bun', 'run', 'serve'], {\n       detached: true,\n       stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe']\n     });\n     writePidFile(child.pid);\n     process.exit(0);\n   }\n   ```\n\n2. Write PID to .kspec/.daemon.pid on daemon start\n\n3. Implement stop command: read PID, send SIGTERM, wait, remove PID file\n\n4. Handle orphaned PID files (process not running)\n\n### ACs Covered\n- ac-9: --daemon detaches, writes PID\n- ac-10: stop shuts down, removes PID\n\n### Files to Create/Modify\n- packages/daemon/src/daemon.ts\n- packages/daemon/src/pid.ts\n[2026-01-23T10:38:56.203Z] @claude:\nImplementation plan:\n1. Create src/cli/commands/serve.ts with Commander subcommands:\n   - 'kspec serve' (foreground mode, default port 3456)\n   - 'kspec serve --daemon' (background mode with PID file)\n   - 'kspec serve stop' (graceful shutdown)\n2. Implement daemon/pid.ts for PID file management:\n   - writePidFile() - write PID to .kspec/.daemon.pid\n   - readPidFile() - read existing PID\n   - removePidFile() - cleanup on shutdown\n   - isProcessRunning() - check if PID is alive\n3. Implement daemon detach logic:\n   - Use Bun's subprocess spawn with detached:true\n   - Redirect stdout/stderr to .kspec/.daemon.log\n   - Parent process exits after confirming child started\n4. Integrate with existing server.ts shutdown handler:\n   - Call removePidFile() during graceful shutdown\n5. Add E2E tests for daemon lifecycle\n[2026-01-23T10:41:36.853Z] @claude:\nImplementation progress:\n✅ Created PidFileManager class (packages/daemon/src/pid.ts) with write/read/remove/isProcessRunning methods\n✅ Integrated PID management into server.ts (write on daemon start, remove on shutdown)\n✅ Created serve command structure (src/cli/commands/serve.ts) with serve/stop subcommands\n✅ Created comprehensive E2E tests for PID file lifecycle (tests/daemon-pid.test.ts)\n\n⚠️ Issue discovered: TypeScript compilation error - CLI (in src/) trying to import daemon (in packages/) causes rootDir conflict. The daemon package is separate with its own build.\n\nSolution options:\n1. Make serve command dev-only (check for daemon source, not built)\n2. Create separate CLI entry point in daemon package\n3. Move serve logic entirely to daemon package, expose via exported function\n\nNext: Fix TypeScript build errors and complete integration.\n[2026-01-23T10:42:18.033Z] @claude:\nCommit 30487fc: PID file management complete.\n\nImplemented:\n- PidFileManager class with write/read/remove/isProcessRunning\n- Server integration (write PID on daemon start, remove on shutdown)\n- 11 E2E tests covering all PID lifecycle scenarios\n\nRemaining work:\n- CLI command for 'kspec serve' and 'kspec serve stop' (should live in daemon package, not src/cli)\n- Process detach implementation using spawn() with detached:true\n- Log file redirection (.kspec/.daemon.log)\n- Integration tests for full daemon start/stop lifecycle\n\nStatus: Core PID management done. CLI integration blocked by package boundary issue - needs architectural decision on where serve command lives.\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-json-output ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: command supports JSON mode\n    When: --json flag is provided\n    Then: output is valid JSON with no ANSI color codes\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON mode is active\n    When: command completes successfully\n    Then: output includes all data available in human-readable mode\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON mode is active\n    When: command encounters an error\n    Then: error is returned as JSON object with error field\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON output contains references\n    When: output is generated\n    Then: references use @ prefix consistently\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON output contains timestamps\n    When: output is generated\n    Then: timestamps use ISO 8601 format\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: command supports --json\n    When: used with other formatting flags\n    Then: --json takes precedence over other format options\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-error-guidance ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: command encounters error\n    When: error message is shown\n    Then: includes description of what went wrong\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: command encounters error\n    When: error message is shown\n    Then: includes suggested action to resolve\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: reference not found\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: suggests checking ref with kspec search or kspec <type> list\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: invalid state transition\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: indicates current state and valid next states\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: validation error\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: indicates which field/value failed validation\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: error in JSON mode\n    When: --json is active\n    Then: guidance included in structured error object\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-shadow-commit ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: command modifies state in shadow worktree\n    When: save operation completes successfully\n    Then: git commit is created in shadow branch with semantic message\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow commit is created\n    When: commit message is generated\n    Then: message follows pattern operation-colon-ref-short with optional detail\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow commit is created\n    When: item reference is available\n    Then: commit message includes ULID prefix (8 chars) or primary slug\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow is not configured (no worktree)\n    When: command that would normally commit runs\n    Then: command completes successfully without attempting git operations\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: save operation fails\n    When: validation or IO error occurs\n    Then: no commit is attempted and error is returned\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow has remote configured\n    When: commit succeeds\n    Then: push is attempted in fire-and-forget mode (failure doesn't block command)\n  [ac-7] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: commit or push fails\n    When: save succeeded but git operation failed\n    Then: command succeeds but outputs warning about sync state\n  [ac-8] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: command performs multiple related saves\n    When: all saves complete successfully\n    Then: single atomic commit covers all changes\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-localhost-security ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-localhost-security)\n    Given: server is starting\n    When: binding to network interface\n    Then: only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-localhost-security)\n    Given: connection attempt from non-localhost\n    When: request received\n    Then: connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-localhost-security)\n    Given: server is configured\n    When: configuration allows external binding\n    Then: warning displayed about security implications\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-websocket-protocol ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: WebSocket connection is established\n    When: client connects\n    Then: server assigns unique connection ID and sends connected event with session_id\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: client wants notifications\n    When: subscribe command sent with topics array\n    Then: server tracks subscription and sends ack with request_id\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: client is subscribed to topic\n    When: relevant change occurs\n    Then: server broadcasts event with format {msg_id, seq, timestamp, topic, event, data}\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: WebSocket connection is active\n    When: 30 seconds pass without activity\n    Then: server sends ping frame\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: ping was sent\n    When: no pong received within 90 seconds\n    Then: connection is closed with code 1001\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: server sends events\n    When: client cannot keep up (backpressure)\n    Then: server pauses non-critical broadcasts until drain event\n  [ac-7] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: connection is closing\n    When: close initiated\n    Then: use code 1000 for clean close, 1001 for timeout, 1011 for error\n  [ac-8] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: client reconnects after disconnect\n    When: new connection established\n    Then: client resets sequence tracking (lastSeqProcessed = -1) since server generates new sequence","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false},"toolName":"Bash"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_01PgYbt2wMhM1je2QfHkxnkC","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update"}}}
./sessions/01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP/events.jsonl:{"ts":1769165246335,"seq":23204,"type":"session.update","session_id":"01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP","data":{"iteration":10,"update":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"toolName":"Bash"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_01PgYbt2wMhM1je2QfHkxnkC","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"Implement daemon process detach\n────────────────────────────────────────\nULID:      01KFMMMH7B711BQZ8WFT4PVQT4\nType:      task\nStatus:    pending_review\nPriority:  2\nAutomation: eligible\nSpec ref:  @daemon-server\nTags:      phase-1, daemon\nCreated:   2026-01-23T05:18:37.290Z\nStarted:   2026-01-23T10:38:36.162Z\n\n─── Spec Context ───\nDaemon Server Mode\nType: feature\nImplementation: in_progress\nDescription:\n  Long-running Elysia.js server on Bun runtime that exposes kspec state via HTTP API and WebSocket\n  for real-time updates. Binds to localhost only for security. Supports foreground and background\n  modes with PID file management. Includes heartbeat ping/pong for connection health monitoring.\nAcceptance Criteria:\n  [ac-1]\n    Given: kspec is installed\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve'\n    Then: Elysia HTTP server starts on configurable port (default 3456) binding to localhost only\n  [ac-2]\n    Given: daemon is starting\n    When: server binds to network interface\n    Then: only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\n  [ac-3]\n    Given: connection attempt from non-localhost IP\n    When: request received\n    Then: connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\n  [ac-4]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: any .kspec/*.yaml file changes\n    Then: connected WebSocket clients receive update event via topic subscription\n  [ac-5]\n    Given: file watching is active\n    When: rapid changes occur (< 500ms apart)\n    Then: events are debounced and aggregated into single notification\n  [ac-6]\n    Given: watched file has YAML parse error\n    When: change detected\n    Then: error logged and WebSocket broadcasts error event (daemon does not crash)\n  [ac-7]\n    Given: .kspec directory becomes inaccessible\n    When: watcher encounters error\n    Then: daemon logs error and attempts recovery with exponential backoff\n  [ac-8]\n    Given: Bun fs.watch fails or misses events\n    When: reliability issue detected\n    Then: automatically fall back to Chokidar file watcher\n  [ac-9]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve --daemon'\n    Then: process detaches to background, writes PID to .kspec/.daemon.pid, CLI returns immediately\n  [ac-10]\n    Given: daemon is running in background\n    When: user runs 'kspec serve stop'\n    Then: daemon shuts down gracefully, removes PID file, closes all WebSocket connections\n  [ac-11]\n    Given: daemon is running\n    When: GET /api/health is called\n    Then: returns {status, uptime, connections, version} JSON\n  [ac-12]\n    Given: daemon receives SIGTERM or SIGINT\n    When: shutdown signal received\n    Then: graceful shutdown (flush pending messages, close connections, save state)\n  [ac-13]\n    Given: WebSocket connection established\n    When: 30 seconds pass without activity\n    Then: server sends ping frame\n  [ac-14]\n    Given: ping was sent\n    When: no pong received within 90 seconds\n    Then: connection closed with code 1001\n  [ac-15]\n    Given: Elysia server is configured\n    When: routes are registered\n    Then: use plugin pattern for middleware (CORS, logging, validation)\n  [ac-16]\n    Given: daemon code is ready\n    When: bun build --compile runs\n    Then: produces standalone executable without requiring Bun installation\n\n─── Notes ───\n[2026-01-23T05:19:36.801Z] @claude:\n## Implementation Notes\n\n### Objective\nImplement daemon background mode with process detach, PID file management.\n\n### Steps\n1. Implement --daemon flag handling:\n   ```typescript\n   if (args.daemon) {\n     const child = Bun.spawn(['bun', 'run', 'serve'], {\n       detached: true,\n       stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe']\n     });\n     writePidFile(child.pid);\n     process.exit(0);\n   }\n   ```\n\n2. Write PID to .kspec/.daemon.pid on daemon start\n\n3. Implement stop command: read PID, send SIGTERM, wait, remove PID file\n\n4. Handle orphaned PID files (process not running)\n\n### ACs Covered\n- ac-9: --daemon detaches, writes PID\n- ac-10: stop shuts down, removes PID\n\n### Files to Create/Modify\n- packages/daemon/src/daemon.ts\n- packages/daemon/src/pid.ts\n[2026-01-23T10:38:56.203Z] @claude:\nImplementation plan:\n1. Create src/cli/commands/serve.ts with Commander subcommands:\n   - 'kspec serve' (foreground mode, default port 3456)\n   - 'kspec serve --daemon' (background mode with PID file)\n   - 'kspec serve stop' (graceful shutdown)\n2. Implement daemon/pid.ts for PID file management:\n   - writePidFile() - write PID to .kspec/.daemon.pid\n   - readPidFile() - read existing PID\n   - removePidFile() - cleanup on shutdown\n   - isProcessRunning() - check if PID is alive\n3. Implement daemon detach logic:\n   - Use Bun's subprocess spawn with detached:true\n   - Redirect stdout/stderr to .kspec/.daemon.log\n   - Parent process exits after confirming child started\n4. Integrate with existing server.ts shutdown handler:\n   - Call removePidFile() during graceful shutdown\n5. Add E2E tests for daemon lifecycle\n[2026-01-23T10:41:36.853Z] @claude:\nImplementation progress:\n✅ Created PidFileManager class (packages/daemon/src/pid.ts) with write/read/remove/isProcessRunning methods\n✅ Integrated PID management into server.ts (write on daemon start, remove on shutdown)\n✅ Created serve command structure (src/cli/commands/serve.ts) with serve/stop subcommands\n✅ Created comprehensive E2E tests for PID file lifecycle (tests/daemon-pid.test.ts)\n\n⚠️ Issue discovered: TypeScript compilation error - CLI (in src/) trying to import daemon (in packages/) causes rootDir conflict. The daemon package is separate with its own build.\n\nSolution options:\n1. Make serve command dev-only (check for daemon source, not built)\n2. Create separate CLI entry point in daemon package\n3. Move serve logic entirely to daemon package, expose via exported function\n\nNext: Fix TypeScript build errors and complete integration.\n[2026-01-23T10:42:18.033Z] @claude:\nCommit 30487fc: PID file management complete.\n\nImplemented:\n- PidFileManager class with write/read/remove/isProcessRunning\n- Server integration (write PID on daemon start, remove on shutdown)\n- 11 E2E tests covering all PID lifecycle scenarios\n\nRemaining work:\n- CLI command for 'kspec serve' and 'kspec serve stop' (should live in daemon package, not src/cli)\n- Process detach implementation using spawn() with detached:true\n- Log file redirection (.kspec/.daemon.log)\n- Integration tests for full daemon start/stop lifecycle\n\nStatus: Core PID management done. CLI integration blocked by package boundary issue - needs architectural decision on where serve command lives.\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-json-output ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: command supports JSON mode\n    When: --json flag is provided\n    Then: output is valid JSON with no ANSI color codes\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON mode is active\n    When: command completes successfully\n    Then: output includes all data available in human-readable mode\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON mode is active\n    When: command encounters an error\n    Then: error is returned as JSON object with error field\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON output contains references\n    When: output is generated\n    Then: references use @ prefix consistently\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: JSON output contains timestamps\n    When: output is generated\n    Then: timestamps use ISO 8601 format\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-json-output)\n    Given: command supports --json\n    When: used with other formatting flags\n    Then: --json takes precedence over other format options\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-error-guidance ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: command encounters error\n    When: error message is shown\n    Then: includes description of what went wrong\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: command encounters error\n    When: error message is shown\n    Then: includes suggested action to resolve\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: reference not found\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: suggests checking ref with kspec search or kspec <type> list\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: invalid state transition\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: indicates current state and valid next states\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: validation error\n    When: error is shown\n    Then: indicates which field/value failed validation\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-error-guidance)\n    Given: error in JSON mode\n    When: --json is active\n    Then: guidance included in structured error object\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-shadow-commit ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: command modifies state in shadow worktree\n    When: save operation completes successfully\n    Then: git commit is created in shadow branch with semantic message\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow commit is created\n    When: commit message is generated\n    Then: message follows pattern operation-colon-ref-short with optional detail\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow commit is created\n    When: item reference is available\n    Then: commit message includes ULID prefix (8 chars) or primary slug\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow is not configured (no worktree)\n    When: command that would normally commit runs\n    Then: command completes successfully without attempting git operations\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: save operation fails\n    When: validation or IO error occurs\n    Then: no commit is attempted and error is returned\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: shadow has remote configured\n    When: commit succeeds\n    Then: push is attempted in fire-and-forget mode (failure doesn't block command)\n  [ac-7] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: commit or push fails\n    When: save succeeded but git operation failed\n    Then: command succeeds but outputs warning about sync state\n  [ac-8] (from @trait-shadow-commit)\n    Given: command performs multiple related saves\n    When: all saves complete successfully\n    Then: single atomic commit covers all changes\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-localhost-security ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-localhost-security)\n    Given: server is starting\n    When: binding to network interface\n    Then: only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-localhost-security)\n    Given: connection attempt from non-localhost\n    When: request received\n    Then: connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-localhost-security)\n    Given: server is configured\n    When: configuration allows external binding\n    Then: warning displayed about security implications\n\n─── Inherited from @trait-websocket-protocol ───\n  [ac-1] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: WebSocket connection is established\n    When: client connects\n    Then: server assigns unique connection ID and sends connected event with session_id\n  [ac-2] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: client wants notifications\n    When: subscribe command sent with topics array\n    Then: server tracks subscription and sends ack with request_id\n  [ac-3] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: client is subscribed to topic\n    When: relevant change occurs\n    Then: server broadcasts event with format {msg_id, seq, timestamp, topic, event, data}\n  [ac-4] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: WebSocket connection is active\n    When: 30 seconds pass without activity\n    Then: server sends ping frame\n  [ac-5] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: ping was sent\n    When: no pong received within 90 seconds\n    Then: connection is closed with code 1001\n  [ac-6] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: server sends events\n    When: client cannot keep up (backpressure)\n    Then: server pauses non-critical broadcasts until drain event\n  [ac-7] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: connection is closing\n    When: close initiated\n    Then: use code 1000 for clean close, 1001 for timeout, 1011 for error\n  [ac-8] (from @trait-websocket-protocol)\n    Given: client reconnects after disconnect\n    When: new connection established\n    Then: client resets sequence tracking (lastSeqProcessed = -1) since server generates new sequence"}}]}}}
./sessions/01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP/events.jsonl:{"ts":1769165294210,"seq":23205,"type":"session.update","session_id":"01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP","data":{"iteration":10,"update":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"toolResponse":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Run /local-review for PR #188. Check AC coverage, test quality, E2E preference, and test isolation.","agentId":"a764f1a","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have enough information. Let me compile the local review report.\n\n---\n\n# Local Review Report - PR #188\n\n**PR:** feat: implement PID file management for daemon lifecycle  \n**Spec:** @daemon-server  \n**Task:** @01KFMMMH  \n**Branch:** feat/daemon-pid-management\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR implements the foundation for daemon process lifecycle management by adding PID file operations. It provides **partial** coverage of AC-9 and AC-10 from the @daemon-server spec. The implementation is high quality with good test coverage, but the actual acceptance criteria are not yet fully met.\n\n---\n\n## 1. AC Coverage Analysis\n\n### AC-9: Daemon Process Detach\n**Status:** ⚠️ **PARTIAL - ADVISORY**\n\n**Acceptance Criterion:**\n> Given: daemon is running  \n> When: user runs 'kspec serve --daemon'  \n> Then: process detaches to background, writes PID to .kspec/.daemon.pid, CLI returns immediately\n\n**What's Implemented:**\n- ✅ PID file write functionality (`PidFileManager.write()`)\n- ✅ Server integration to write PID when `isDaemon: true`\n- ✅ Tests for PID file write operations\n\n**What's Missing:**\n- ❌ No `kspec serve` CLI command\n- ❌ No `--daemon` flag handling\n- ❌ No process detach implementation\n- ❌ No \"CLI returns immediately\" behavior\n- ❌ No E2E test that validates the actual AC (user running the command)\n\n**Current Tests:**\n```typescript\n// AC: @daemon-server ac-9\nit('should write current process PID to file', () => {\n  const pidManager = new PidFileManager(tempDir);\n  pidManager.write();\n  // ... validates PID file exists and contains correct PID\n});\n```\n\nThese tests validate the PidFileManager **class**, but not the actual AC which is about the `kspec serve --daemon` **command**.\n\n### AC-10: Daemon Graceful Shutdown\n**Status:** ⚠️ **PARTIAL - ADVISORY**\n\n**Acceptance Criterion:**\n> Given: daemon is running in background  \n> When: user runs 'kspec serve stop'  \n> Then: daemon shuts down gracefully, removes PID file, closes all WebSocket connections\n\n**What's Implemented:**\n- ✅ PID file removal functionality (`PidFileManager.remove()`)\n- ✅ Server integration to remove PID on SIGTERM/SIGINT shutdown\n- ✅ Tests for PID file removal operations\n\n**What's Missing:**\n- ❌ No `kspec serve stop` CLI command\n- ❌ No mechanism to send shutdown signal to background daemon\n- ❌ No E2E test that validates the actual AC (user running the command)\n\n**Current Tests:**\n```typescript\n// AC: @daemon-server ac-10\nit('should remove PID file', () => {\n  const pidManager = new PidFileManager(tempDir);\n  pidManager.write();\n  pidManager.remove();\n  expect(existsSync(pidFilePath)).toBe(false);\n});\n```\n\nAgain, these tests validate the **class methods**, not the **user-facing behavior** described in the AC.\n\n### Other ACs\nThis PR does not address other acceptance criteria for @daemon-server (ac-1 through ac-8, ac-11 through ac-16).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Test Quality: ✅ PASS\n\nAll 11 tests are **high quality** and properly validate their intended purpose.\n\n**Strengths:**\n- ✅ Each test validates real behavior (not fluff)\n- ✅ Tests cover happy path, error handling, and edge cases\n- ✅ Clear test names describing what's being validated\n- ✅ Proper AC annotations on every test\n\n**Test Coverage:**\n- PID file write/read/remove operations\n- Invalid/missing PID file handling\n- Process running detection\n- Daemon state detection (running vs stale vs absent)\n\n**Example of a well-written test:**\n```typescript\n// AC: @daemon-server ac-10\nit('should detect daemon not running when PID file stale', () => {\n  const pidManager = new PidFileManager(tempDir);\n  \n  // Write a PID that doesn't exist\n  writeFileSync(join(tempDir, '.daemon.pid'), '999999', 'utf-8');\n  \n  expect(pidManager.isDaemonRunning()).toBe(false);\n});\n```\n\nThis test would **fail if the feature breaks** (e.g., if `isDaemonRunning()` returned true for stale PIDs).\n\n**No fluff tests detected.**\n\n---\n\n## 3. Test Strategy: ⚠️ ADVISORY\n\n**Current Approach:**\n- Unit tests for `PidFileManager` class methods\n- Tests run in isolated temp directories\n- 11 tests, all passing\n\n**Missing E2E Coverage:**\nThe tests validate the **implementation layer** (class methods) but not the **user interface layer** (CLI commands). \n\n**Recommended Addition (not blocking, but valuable):**\n```typescript\nit('should start daemon in background with --daemon flag', async () => {\n  // E2E test that actually runs: kspec serve --daemon\n  const result = await kspec(['serve', '--daemon'], tempDir);\n  \n  expect(result.exitCode).toBe(0);\n  expect(result.stdout).toContain('Daemon started');\n  \n  const pidFile = await readFile(join(tempDir, '.kspec/.daemon.pid'));\n  const pid = parseInt(pidFile, 10);\n  expect(process.kill(pid, 0)).not.toThrow(); // Process exists\n});\n\nit('should stop daemon with serve stop', async () => {\n  // Start daemon first\n  await kspec(['serve', '--daemon'], tempDir);\n  \n  // Stop it\n  const result = await kspec(['serve', 'stop'], tempDir);\n  \n  expect(result.exitCode).toBe(0);\n  expect(existsSync(join(tempDir, '.kspec/.daemon.pid'))).toBe(false);\n});\n```\n\nThese would be E2E tests that validate the actual ACs. However, they can't be written yet since the CLI commands don't exist.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Test Isolation: ✅ PASS\n\nAll tests properly run in temp directories with full setup/teardown.\n\n```typescript\nlet tempDir: string;\n\nbeforeEach(async () => {\n  tempDir = await createTempDir();\n});\n\nafterEach(async () => {\n  await cleanupTempDir(tempDir);\n});\n```\n\n**Strengths:**\n- ✅ Tests use temp directories, not the actual kspec repo\n- ✅ Proper cleanup after each test\n- ✅ No risk of corrupting `.kspec/` data\n- ✅ Tests are reproducible and isolated\n\n**No isolation issues detected.**\n\n---\n\n## 5. Implementation Quality: ✅ EXCELLENT\n\nThe `PidFileManager` class is well-designed and production-ready:\n\n**Strengths:**\n- ✅ Clear separation of concerns\n- ✅ Proper error handling (returns `null` instead of throwing)\n- ✅ Uses `process.kill(pid, 0)` for process detection (standard Unix pattern)\n- ✅ Handles missing/invalid PID files gracefully\n- ✅ AC annotations in code comments\n- ✅ Proper integration with server shutdown handlers\n\n**Example:**\n```typescript\n// AC: @daemon-server ac-9\nwrite(): void {\n  writeFileSync(this.pidFilePath, process.pid.toString(), 'utf-8');\n}\n\n// AC: @daemon-server ac-10\nremove(): void {\n  if (existsSync(this.pidFilePath)) {\n    unlinkSync(this.pidFilePath);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nClean, simple, correct.\n\n---\n\n## Issue Summary\n\n| Issue | Severity | Description |\n|-------|----------|-------------|\n| AC-9 not fully implemented | **Advisory** | Tests cover PID write operations, but `kspec serve --daemon` command doesn't exist |\n| AC-10 not fully implemented | **Advisory** | Tests cover PID removal, but `kspec serve stop` command doesn't exist |\n| Missing E2E tests | **Advisory** | No tests validating the actual user commands from ACs |\n\n---\n\n## Recommendations\n\n### For This PR: ✅ **APPROVE WITH NOTES**\n\nThis PR can be merged as-is because:\n1. The implementation is high quality and production-ready\n2. All tests pass (1149 total, 11 new)\n3. No blocking issues found\n4. PR description accurately states this is \"partial\" coverage and lists remaining work\n\n### For Follow-up Work:\n\n**MUST-FIX (to fully satisfy AC-9 and AC-10):**\n1. Implement `kspec serve` CLI command\n2. Implement `kspec serve --daemon` flag with process detach\n3. Implement `kspec serve stop` command\n4. Add E2E tests that validate the actual user commands\n\n**Architectural Decision Needed:**\nAs noted in task notes, there's a package boundary issue. The serve command should likely live in `packages/daemon/` with its own CLI entry point, not in `src/cli/`.\n\n**Suggested Next Task:**\nCreate a new task for \"Implement kspec serve CLI with daemon mode\" that references @daemon-server ac-9 and ac-10, depending on this PR's completion.\n\n---\n\n## Verdict\n\n**✅ READY TO MERGE**\n\nThis is a well-executed foundation PR. While it doesn't fully implement AC-9 and AC-10, it provides the necessary infrastructure and is correctly labeled as \"partial\" coverage. The quality bar is high across all dimensions:\n- Test quality: Excellent\n- Test isolation: Perfect\n- Implementation: Production-ready\n- Documentation: Clear about scope and next steps\n\nThe missing CLI commands are explicitly called out as \"Next Steps\" in the PR description and task notes, indicating this is intentional incremental progress rather than incomplete work."}],"totalDurationMs":114955,"totalTokens":42117,"totalToolUseCount":17,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3529,"cache_read_input_tokens":36157,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3529,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2428,"service_tier":"standard"}},"toolName":"Task"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_01XkTCSCTFM82q1d8AxG1UQA","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update"}}}
