./sessions/01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP/events.jsonl:{"ts":1769177216308,"seq":42114,"type":"session.update","session_id":"01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP","data":{"iteration":24,"update":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"toolResponse":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Run /local-review for PR #196. Check AC coverage, test quality, E2E preference, and test isolation.","agentId":"a92529a","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me compile the complete review report:\n\n## Local Review Report - PR #196: Create Shared Types Package\n\n### Overview\n**PR:** #196 - Create shared types package  \n**Branch:** `feat/shared-types-package`  \n**Task:** `@01KFMMJY` (Create shared types package)  \n**Spec:** `@web-ui` (Web UI System) / `@api-contract` (REST and WebSocket API Contract)  \n**CI Status:** Test job IN_PROGRESS, Claude review PASSED, Unresolved comments check PASSED\n\n---\n\n## 1. AC Coverage Analysis\n\n### ACs Covered (Type Definitions)\n\nThe implementation provides **type definitions** for the following acceptance criteria:\n\n**API Response Types** (`api.ts`):\n- ✅ **ac-2**: TaskSummary for list endpoints\n- ✅ **ac-4**: PaginatedResponse wrapper\n- ✅ **ac-5**: TaskDetail with notes and todos\n- ✅ **ac-8**: ItemSummary for list endpoints\n- ✅ **ac-10**: ItemDetail with ACs and traits\n- ✅ **ac-12**: InboxItem\n- ✅ **ac-15**: SessionContext\n- ✅ **ac-16**: Agent\n- ✅ **ac-17**: Workflow\n- ✅ **ac-18**: Observation\n- ✅ **ac-19**: SearchResult\n- ✅ **ac-20**: ValidationResult\n- ✅ **ac-21**: AlignmentStats\n- ✅ **ac-22, ac-23, ac-24**: ErrorResponse\n\n**WebSocket Protocol Types** (`websocket.ts`):\n- ✅ **ac-25**: ConnectedEvent with session_id\n- ✅ **ac-26**: WebSocketCommand format\n- ✅ **ac-27**: CommandAck format\n- ✅ **ac-29**: BroadcastEvent with seq\n\n**Total Coverage:** 18 ACs have type definitions  \n**Annotation Quality:** All types properly annotated with `// AC: @api-contract ac-N` comments\n\n### ACs NOT Covered (Implementation Required)\n\nThe following ACs require **runtime implementation** in the daemon, not just types:\n\n**API Behavior** (daemon implementation needed):\n- ❌ **ac-1**: CORS headers\n- ❌ **ac-3**: Status filtering (multi-value)\n- ❌ **ac-6**: POST /api/tasks/:ref/start\n- ❌ **ac-7**: POST /api/tasks/:ref/note\n- ❌ **ac-9**: Type filtering\n- ❌ **ac-11**: GET /api/items/:ref/tasks\n- ❌ **ac-13**: POST /api/inbox\n- ❌ **ac-14**: DELETE /api/inbox/:ref\n\n**WebSocket Behavior** (daemon implementation needed):\n- ❌ **ac-28**: Subscribe command handling\n- ❌ **ac-30**: Malformed command handling\n- ❌ **ac-31**: Close codes\n- ❌ **ac-32**: Backpressure handling\n- ❌ **ac-33**: Graceful shutdown\n\n### Assessment: **ACCEPTABLE** ✅\n\n**Rationale:** This is a **types-only package**. The task is to create shared TypeScript types for the API contract, not to implement the full API. The 18 ACs that have type definitions are appropriate for this scope. The remaining ACs require daemon implementation and are correctly out of scope for this PR.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Test Quality Analysis\n\n### Current State: **NO TESTS** ❌\n\n**Finding:** Zero test files exist for the shared package.\n\n**Expected Tests:**\n1. **Type validation tests** - Ensure types compile correctly\n2. **Type compatibility tests** - Verify types match Zod schemas\n3. **Export integrity tests** - Confirm all types are properly exported\n\n### Critical Issue: **MUST-FIX**\n\nThis is a **types-only package** with no runtime behavior, which presents a special case:\n\n**Standard approach would require:**\n- TypeScript compilation tests (verify types are valid)\n- Type compatibility tests (ensure types match Zod schemas in main package)\n- Export tests (verify all types are accessible)\n\n**However**, the PR description states:\n> **Test Plan**\n> - [x] Package builds successfully (`npm run build`)\n> - [x] Typechecks pass (`npm run typecheck`)\n\nThe build and typecheck passing provides **minimal validation** that:\n- Types are syntactically valid\n- No TypeScript errors exist\n- Exports are structurally correct\n\n### Recommended Actions (MUST-FIX):\n\n**Option 1 - Add Minimal Type Tests** (Preferred):\n```typescript\n// packages/shared/src/__tests__/types.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expectTypeOf } from 'vitest';\nimport type { TaskSummary, PaginatedResponse, WebSocketCommand } from '../index.js';\n\ndescribe('Type exports', () => {\n  // AC: @api-contract ac-2\n  it('should export TaskSummary with correct shape', () => {\n    expectTypeOf<TaskSummary>().toMatchTypeOf<{\n      _ulid: string;\n      title: string;\n      status: string;\n    }>();\n  });\n\n  // AC: @api-contract ac-4\n  it('should export PaginatedResponse as generic wrapper', () => {\n    expectTypeOf<PaginatedResponse<TaskSummary>>().toMatchTypeOf<{\n      items: TaskSummary[];\n      total: number;\n    }>();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**Option 2 - Document Why Tests Are Skipped**:\nAdd a `TESTING.md` in the package explaining why runtime tests aren't applicable for a pure types package, and what validation is performed (build + typecheck).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Test Strategy Analysis\n\n### Assessment: **NOT APPLICABLE** ⚠️\n\n**Rationale:** This is a pure TypeScript types package with:\n- No runtime behavior to test\n- No functions or logic to execute\n- No E2E scenarios possible\n\n**What validates correctness:**\n1. ✅ TypeScript compiler (via `npm run build`)\n2. ✅ Type checker (via `npm run typecheck`)\n3. ⏳ Integration tests in **daemon** that import and use these types\n\n**Recommendation:** E2E testing will occur in the daemon implementation when these types are consumed. This is the correct approach for a shared types library.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Test Isolation Analysis\n\n### Assessment: **NOT APPLICABLE** ⚠️\n\n**Rationale:** No tests exist, so isolation is not a concern. When/if tests are added, they should follow the pattern of using `vitest` type tests which don't require temp directories.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Additional Quality Checks\n\n### ✅ **Code Annotations Present**\n- All types properly annotated with `// AC: @api-contract ac-N`\n- Clear documentation comments explaining purpose\n- AC coverage clearly traceable\n\n### ✅ **Build Configuration**\n- `tsconfig.json` properly configured\n- `.d.ts` declaration files generated\n- Source maps included\n\n### ✅ **Package Structure**\n- Clean exports via `index.ts`\n- Organized by domain (api, websocket, schemas)\n- No unnecessary dependencies (Zod removed per review feedback)\n\n### ⚠️ **Type Alignment with Zod Schemas**\n**Concern:** The PR description states types are \"aligned with Zod schemas\" but there's no automated verification of this alignment.\n\n**Recommendation:** Consider adding a script or test that:\n1. Imports Zod schemas from main package\n2. Uses `z.infer<typeof schema>` to extract types\n3. Validates shared types match inferred types\n\nExample:\n```typescript\nimport { expectTypeOf } from 'vitest';\nimport { TaskSchema } from '../../src/schema/task.js';\nimport { TaskSummary } from '@kynetic-ai/shared';\n\ntype InferredTask = z.infer<typeof TaskSchema>;\nexpectTypeOf<TaskSummary>().toMatchTypeOf<InferredTask>();\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n### Blocking Issues (MUST-FIX)\n\n1. **NO TESTS** - Zero test coverage for a new package\n   - **Severity:** High for production, Medium for types-only package\n   - **Action:** Add minimal type validation tests OR document why tests are not applicable\n   - **Estimated effort:** 1-2 hours\n\n### Advisory Issues\n\n1. **No automated type alignment verification** between shared types and Zod schemas\n   - **Recommendation:** Add type compatibility tests\n   - **Risk:** Types drift from schemas over time\n   - **Priority:** Medium\n\n### Acceptable Deviations\n\n1. **E2E tests not applicable** - Correct for types-only package\n2. **Test isolation not applicable** - No runtime tests exist\n3. **Incomplete AC coverage** - Remaining ACs require daemon implementation (out of scope)\n\n---\n\n## CI Status\n\n- ✅ **Claude Review:** PASSED\n- ✅ **Unresolved Comments Check:** PASSED  \n- ⏳ **Tests:** IN_PROGRESS (currently running)\n\n---\n\n## Final Recommendation\n\n### Current State: **CONDITIONAL APPROVAL** ⚠️\n\n**Recommendation:** **Wait for CI to complete**, then either:\n\n**Path A - Merge with follow-up:** \n- Merge if CI passes\n- Create follow-up task to add type validation tests\n- Document in task notes that tests will be added separately\n\n**Path B - Block until tests added:**\n- Add minimal type validation tests now\n- Verify exports and type shapes\n- Ensures package quality from day one\n\n### Rationale\n\nThis is a **foundation package** that daemon and web-ui will depend on. While it contains only types (no runtime behavior), having **basic type validation tests** ensures:\n- Types compile correctly\n- Exports are accessible\n- Type shapes match expectations\n- Regression protection as types evolve\n\n**Recommendation:** Take **Path B** - add minimal tests before merge. The effort is low (1-2 hours) and establishes good practices for the monorepo.\n\n---\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/shared/src/api.ts` (244 lines)\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/shared/src/websocket.ts` (66 lines)\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/shared/src/schemas.ts` (67 lines)\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/shared/src/index.ts` (15 lines)\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/shared/package.json` (18 lines)\n\n**Total:** 410 lines of implementation, 0 lines of tests"}],"totalDurationMs":104292,"totalTokens":36155,"totalToolUseCount":18,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":585,"cache_read_input_tokens":32940,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":585,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2628,"service_tier":"standard"}},"toolName":"Task"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_01U8VPFQom3E38kfRbPsovfS","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update"}}}
./sessions/01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP/events.jsonl:{"ts":1769177216344,"seq":42115,"type":"session.update","session_id":"01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP","data":{"iteration":24,"update":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"toolName":"Task"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_01U8VPFQom3E38kfRbPsovfS","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me compile the complete review report:\n\n## Local Review Report - PR #196: Create Shared Types Package\n\n### Overview\n**PR:** #196 - Create shared types package  \n**Branch:** `feat/shared-types-package`  \n**Task:** `@01KFMMJY` (Create shared types package)  \n**Spec:** `@web-ui` (Web UI System) / `@api-contract` (REST and WebSocket API Contract)  \n**CI Status:** Test job IN_PROGRESS, Claude review PASSED, Unresolved comments check PASSED\n\n---\n\n## 1. AC Coverage Analysis\n\n### ACs Covered (Type Definitions)\n\nThe implementation provides **type definitions** for the following acceptance criteria:\n\n**API Response Types** (`api.ts`):\n- ✅ **ac-2**: TaskSummary for list endpoints\n- ✅ **ac-4**: PaginatedResponse wrapper\n- ✅ **ac-5**: TaskDetail with notes and todos\n- ✅ **ac-8**: ItemSummary for list endpoints\n- ✅ **ac-10**: ItemDetail with ACs and traits\n- ✅ **ac-12**: InboxItem\n- ✅ **ac-15**: SessionContext\n- ✅ **ac-16**: Agent\n- ✅ **ac-17**: Workflow\n- ✅ **ac-18**: Observation\n- ✅ **ac-19**: SearchResult\n- ✅ **ac-20**: ValidationResult\n- ✅ **ac-21**: AlignmentStats\n- ✅ **ac-22, ac-23, ac-24**: ErrorResponse\n\n**WebSocket Protocol Types** (`websocket.ts`):\n- ✅ **ac-25**: ConnectedEvent with session_id\n- ✅ **ac-26**: WebSocketCommand format\n- ✅ **ac-27**: CommandAck format\n- ✅ **ac-29**: BroadcastEvent with seq\n\n**Total Coverage:** 18 ACs have type definitions  \n**Annotation Quality:** All types properly annotated with `// AC: @api-contract ac-N` comments\n\n### ACs NOT Covered (Implementation Required)\n\nThe following ACs require **runtime implementation** in the daemon, not just types:\n\n**API Behavior** (daemon implementation needed):\n- ❌ **ac-1**: CORS headers\n- ❌ **ac-3**: Status filtering (multi-value)\n- ❌ **ac-6**: POST /api/tasks/:ref/start\n- ❌ **ac-7**: POST /api/tasks/:ref/note\n- ❌ **ac-9**: Type filtering\n- ❌ **ac-11**: GET /api/items/:ref/tasks\n- ❌ **ac-13**: POST /api/inbox\n- ❌ **ac-14**: DELETE /api/inbox/:ref\n\n**WebSocket Behavior** (daemon implementation needed):\n- ❌ **ac-28**: Subscribe command handling\n- ❌ **ac-30**: Malformed command handling\n- ❌ **ac-31**: Close codes\n- ❌ **ac-32**: Backpressure handling\n- ❌ **ac-33**: Graceful shutdown\n\n### Assessment: **ACCEPTABLE** ✅\n\n**Rationale:** This is a **types-only package**. The task is to create shared TypeScript types for the API contract, not to implement the full API. The 18 ACs that have type definitions are appropriate for this scope. The remaining ACs require daemon implementation and are correctly out of scope for this PR.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Test Quality Analysis\n\n### Current State: **NO TESTS** ❌\n\n**Finding:** Zero test files exist for the shared package.\n\n**Expected Tests:**\n1. **Type validation tests** - Ensure types compile correctly\n2. **Type compatibility tests** - Verify types match Zod schemas\n3. **Export integrity tests** - Confirm all types are properly exported\n\n### Critical Issue: **MUST-FIX**\n\nThis is a **types-only package** with no runtime behavior, which presents a special case:\n\n**Standard approach would require:**\n- TypeScript compilation tests (verify types are valid)\n- Type compatibility tests (ensure types match Zod schemas in main package)\n- Export tests (verify all types are accessible)\n\n**However**, the PR description states:\n> **Test Plan**\n> - [x] Package builds successfully (`npm run build`)\n> - [x] Typechecks pass (`npm run typecheck`)\n\nThe build and typecheck passing provides **minimal validation** that:\n- Types are syntactically valid\n- No TypeScript errors exist\n- Exports are structurally correct\n\n### Recommended Actions (MUST-FIX):\n\n**Option 1 - Add Minimal Type Tests** (Preferred):\n```typescript\n// packages/shared/src/__tests__/types.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expectTypeOf } from 'vitest';\nimport type { TaskSummary, PaginatedResponse, WebSocketCommand } from '../index.js';\n\ndescribe('Type exports', () => {\n  // AC: @api-contract ac-2\n  it('should export TaskSummary with correct shape', () => {\n    expectTypeOf<TaskSummary>().toMatchTypeOf<{\n      _ulid: string;\n      title: string;\n      status: string;\n    }>();\n  });\n\n  // AC: @api-contract ac-4\n  it('should export PaginatedResponse as generic wrapper', () => {\n    expectTypeOf<PaginatedResponse<TaskSummary>>().toMatchTypeOf<{\n      items: TaskSummary[];\n      total: number;\n    }>();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**Option 2 - Document Why Tests Are Skipped**:\nAdd a `TESTING.md` in the package explaining why runtime tests aren't applicable for a pure types package, and what validation is performed (build + typecheck).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Test Strategy Analysis\n\n### Assessment: **NOT APPLICABLE** ⚠️\n\n**Rationale:** This is a pure TypeScript types package with:\n- No runtime behavior to test\n- No functions or logic to execute\n- No E2E scenarios possible\n\n**What validates correctness:**\n1. ✅ TypeScript compiler (via `npm run build`)\n2. ✅ Type checker (via `npm run typecheck`)\n3. ⏳ Integration tests in **daemon** that import and use these types\n\n**Recommendation:** E2E testing will occur in the daemon implementation when these types are consumed. This is the correct approach for a shared types library.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Test Isolation Analysis\n\n### Assessment: **NOT APPLICABLE** ⚠️\n\n**Rationale:** No tests exist, so isolation is not a concern. When/if tests are added, they should follow the pattern of using `vitest` type tests which don't require temp directories.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Additional Quality Checks\n\n### ✅ **Code Annotations Present**\n- All types properly annotated with `// AC: @api-contract ac-N`\n- Clear documentation comments explaining purpose\n- AC coverage clearly traceable\n\n### ✅ **Build Configuration**\n- `tsconfig.json` properly configured\n- `.d.ts` declaration files generated\n- Source maps included\n\n### ✅ **Package Structure**\n- Clean exports via `index.ts`\n- Organized by domain (api, websocket, schemas)\n- No unnecessary dependencies (Zod removed per review feedback)\n\n### ⚠️ **Type Alignment with Zod Schemas**\n**Concern:** The PR description states types are \"aligned with Zod schemas\" but there's no automated verification of this alignment.\n\n**Recommendation:** Consider adding a script or test that:\n1. Imports Zod schemas from main package\n2. Uses `z.infer<typeof schema>` to extract types\n3. Validates shared types match inferred types\n\nExample:\n```typescript\nimport { expectTypeOf } from 'vitest';\nimport { TaskSchema } from '../../src/schema/task.js';\nimport { TaskSummary } from '@kynetic-ai/shared';\n\ntype InferredTask = z.infer<typeof TaskSchema>;\nexpectTypeOf<TaskSummary>().toMatchTypeOf<InferredTask>();\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n### Blocking Issues (MUST-FIX)\n\n1. **NO TESTS** - Zero test coverage for a new package\n   - **Severity:** High for production, Medium for types-only package\n   - **Action:** Add minimal type validation tests OR document why tests are not applicable\n   - **Estimated effort:** 1-2 hours\n\n### Advisory Issues\n\n1. **No automated type alignment verification** between shared types and Zod schemas\n   - **Recommendation:** Add type compatibility tests\n   - **Risk:** Types drift from schemas over time\n   - **Priority:** Medium\n\n### Acceptable Deviations\n\n1. **E2E tests not applicable** - Correct for types-only package\n2. **Test isolation not applicable** - No runtime tests exist\n3. **Incomplete AC coverage** - Remaining ACs require daemon implementation (out of scope)\n\n---\n\n## CI Status\n\n- ✅ **Claude Review:** PASSED\n- ✅ **Unresolved Comments Check:** PASSED  \n- ⏳ **Tests:** IN_PROGRESS (currently running)\n\n---\n\n## Final Recommendation\n\n### Current State: **CONDITIONAL APPROVAL** ⚠️\n\n**Recommendation:** **Wait for CI to complete**, then either:\n\n**Path A - Merge with follow-up:** \n- Merge if CI passes\n- Create follow-up task to add type validation tests\n- Document in task notes that tests will be added separately\n\n**Path B - Block until tests added:**\n- Add minimal type validation tests now\n- Verify exports and type shapes\n- Ensures package quality from day one\n\n### Rationale\n\nThis is a **foundation package** that daemon and web-ui will depend on. While it contains only types (no runtime behavior), having **basic type validation tests** ensures:\n- Types compile correctly\n- Exports are accessible\n- Type shapes match expectations\n- Regression protection as types evolve\n\n**Recommendation:** Take **Path B** - add minimal tests before merge. The effort is low (1-2 hours) and establishes good practices for the monorepo.\n\n---\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/shared/src/api.ts` (244 lines)\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/shared/src/websocket.ts` (66 lines)\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/shared/src/schemas.ts` (67 lines)\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/shared/src/index.ts` (15 lines)\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/shared/package.json` (18 lines)\n\n**Total:** 410 lines of implementation, 0 lines of tests"}},{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a92529a (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)"}}]}}}
./sessions/01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP/events.jsonl:{"ts":1769177499421,"seq":42879,"type":"session.update","session_id":"01KFMQGTTT7WT99FP37J0PXJXP","data":{"iteration":24,"update":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"toolResponse":{"stdout":"OK Started task: 01KFMMJ1\n\n--- Spec Context ---\nImplementing: Web Dashboard\n\nSvelteKit-based web interface for viewing and editing specs, tasks, inbox, and session state.\nUses shadcn-svelte components for accessible UI. Connects to daemon via REST API and WebSocket\nfor real-time updates. Includes WebSocketManager for connection resilience with exponential\nbackoff reconnection and sequence deduplication.\n\n\nAcceptance Criteria (33):\n  [ac-1]\n    Given: daemon is running and browser opens localhost:3456\n    When: page loads\n    Then: dashboard shows task overview with ready, in_progress, pending_review, blocked, completed counts\n  [ac-2]\n    Given: dashboard is displayed\n    When: task counts update on server\n    Then: counts animate to new values without page refresh (WebSocket-driven)\n  [ac-3]\n    Given: dashboard is displayed\n    When: user clicks a task count badge\n    Then: navigates to task list filtered by that status\n  [ac-4]\n    Given: user is viewing task list\n    When: list loads\n    Then: shows task title, status badge, priority indicator, spec_ref link, notes count\n  [ac-5]\n    Given: user is viewing task list\n    When: clicking a task row\n    Then: task detail panel opens showing description, notes (chronological), todos, dependencies\n  [ac-6]\n    Given: user is viewing task detail\n    When: task has spec_ref\n    Then: spec reference is clickable link to spec item detail\n  [ac-7]\n    Given: user is viewing task detail\n    When: user clicks Start Task button\n    Then: POST to /api/tasks/:ref/start, task status updates, UI reflects change\n  [ac-8]\n    Given: user is viewing task detail\n    When: user types in note textarea and clicks Add Note\n    Then: POST to /api/tasks/:ref/note, note appears in list\n  [ac-9]\n    Given: user is viewing task list\n    When: filter controls are visible\n    Then: can filter by status, type, tag, assignee, automation status\n  [ac-10]\n    Given: user applies filter\n    When: filter selection changes\n    Then: URL updates with query params, list updates without full reload\n  [ac-11]\n    Given: user navigates to /items\n    When: spec tree displays\n    Then: shows hierarchical tree with modules > features > requirements, expand/collapse\n  [ac-12]\n    Given: user clicks spec item in tree\n    When: item detail panel opens\n    Then: shows title, description, acceptance criteria (GWT format), traits, implementation status\n  [ac-13]\n    Given: spec item has linked tasks\n    When: viewing item detail\n    Then: Implementation section shows linked tasks with their status\n  [ac-14]\n    Given: spec item has traits\n    When: viewing item detail\n    Then: Traits section shows trait titles as chips, clickable to trait detail\n  [ac-15]\n    Given: user clicks acceptance criterion\n    When: AC row expands\n    Then: shows full Given/When/Then text with test coverage indicator if available\n  [ac-16]\n    Given: user navigates to /inbox\n    When: inbox list displays\n    Then: shows items ordered by created_at desc with text preview, tags, added_by\n  [ac-17]\n    Given: user clicks Add button\n    When: input field appears\n    Then: user can type text, press Enter to submit\n  [ac-18]\n    Given: new inbox item submitted\n    When: POST succeeds\n    Then: item appears at top of list with animation\n  [ac-19]\n    Given: user clicks delete button on item\n    When: confirmation appears\n    Then: on confirm, item removed from list\n  [ac-20]\n    Given: dashboard header area\n    When: session has focus set\n    Then: displays current focus text prominently\n  [ac-21]\n    Given: dashboard sidebar\n    When: observations exist\n    Then: shows unresolved observations count badge\n  [ac-22]\n    Given: user clicks observations badge\n    When: observations panel opens\n    Then: lists unresolved observations with type icons (friction/success/question/idea)\n  [ac-23]\n    Given: user presses Cmd+K (or Ctrl+K)\n    When: command palette opens\n    Then: shows search input with placeholder\n  [ac-24]\n    Given: user types in search box\n    When: debounced search fires (300ms)\n    Then: results show tasks, items, inbox matching query grouped by type\n  [ac-25]\n    Given: search results display\n    When: user clicks a result\n    Then: navigates to detail view for that item\n  [ac-26]\n    Given: browser width < 768px\n    When: viewing any page\n    Then: layout adapts to single column, sidebar becomes bottom nav\n  [ac-27]\n    Given: browser width >= 1024px\n    When: viewing detail panels\n    Then: detail panel opens as slide-over without navigating away from list\n  [ac-28]\n    Given: WebSocket connection drops\n    When: reconnect logic triggers\n    Then: automatic reconnect with exponential backoff (1s, 2s, 4s... max 30s)\n  [ac-29]\n    Given: WebSocket disconnected for >10s\n    When: viewing dashboard\n    Then: Connection lost indicator shown\n  [ac-30]\n    Given: events received via WebSocket\n    When: seq <= lastSeqProcessed\n    Then: skip duplicate events (sequence deduplication)\n  [ac-31]\n    Given: WebSocket reconnects\n    When: connection established\n    Then: client resets lastSeqProcessed = -1 (server generates new sequence)\n  [ac-32]\n    Given: WebSocket reconnects\n    When: connection established\n    Then: client re-subscribes to all previous topics\n  [ac-33]\n    Given: another client modifies task\n    When: WebSocket update received\n    Then: task list/detail updates without refresh, subtle highlight animation on changed item\n\nRemember: Add test coverage for each AC and mark tests with // AC: @spec-ref ac-N\n\nℹ Synced spec \"Web Dashboard\" implementation: not_started -> in_progress","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false},"toolName":"Bash"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_015HDvoHEKpnFLEJUWizWbiN","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update"}}}
