   465→    description: >\n   466→      Static site generation from kspec state for hosting read-only views on GitHub Pages.\n   467→\n   468→      CI workflow builds JSON snapshot from shadow branch on push, SPA reads this JSON for\n   469→      rendering.\n   470→\n   471→      Enables deep linking to tasks/specs from PRs and issues with data freshness indicator.\n   472→    depends_on: []\n   473→    implements: []\n   474→    relates_to: []\n   475→    tests: []\n   476→    traits:\n   477→      - \"@trait-json-output\"\n   478→      - \"@trait-dry-run\"\n   479→    notes: []\n   480→    created: 2026-01-22T01:18:13.672Z\n   481→    acceptance_criteria:\n   482→      - id: ac-1\n   483→        given: kspec is installed\n   484→        when: user runs 'kspec export --format json'\n   485→        then: writes kspec-snapshot.json containing all tasks, items, inbox, meta to stdout or --output path\n   486→      - id: ac-2\n   487→        given: export runs\n   488→        when: output is generated\n   489→        then: JSON includes exported_at timestamp, version (kspec version), project metadata\n   490→      - id: ac-3\n   491→        given: export runs\n   492→        when: tasks are included\n   493→        then: each task includes resolved spec_ref title (not just ref string) for display without\n   494→          resolution\n   495→      - id: ac-4\n   496→        given: export runs\n   497→        when: items are included\n   498→        then: hierarchical structure preserved, acceptance_criteria expanded, traits resolved to include\n   499→          inherited ACs\n   500→      - id: ac-5\n   501→        given: export runs with --include-validation\n   502→        when: validation is run\n   503→        then: JSON includes validation block with error/warning counts and details\n   504→      - id: ac-6\n   505→        given: kspec is installed\n   506→        when: user runs 'kspec export --format html'\n   507→        then: generates self-contained HTML file with embedded JSON and SPA code\n   508→      - id: ac-7\n   509→        given: kspec is installed\n   510→        when: user runs 'kspec export --dry-run'\n   511→        then: shows what would be exported without writing files\n   512→      - id: ac-8\n   513→        given: push to kspec-meta branch\n   514→        when: CI workflow triggers\n   515→        then: runs kspec export, commits to gh-pages branch\n   516→      - id: ac-9\n   517→        given: CI workflow runs\n   518→        when: SPA assets don't exist\n   519→        then: copies SPA static assets (HTML, JS, CSS) to docs/ alongside JSON\n   520→      - id: ac-10\n   521→        given: rapid commits to kspec-meta\n   522→        when: multiple pushes within 30 seconds\n   523→        then: CI debounces and runs once with latest state\n   524→      - id: ac-11\n   525→        given: user opens gh-pages URL\n   526→        when: SPA loads\n   527→        then: fetches kspec-snapshot.json from same origin, renders dashboard\n   528→      - id: ac-12\n   529→        given: user navigates to /tasks/@task-slug\n   530→        when: deep link resolves\n   531→        then: SPA parses path (history API), shows task detail for that ref\n   532→      - id: ac-13\n   533→        given: user navigates to /items/@spec-slug\n   534→        when: deep link resolves\n   535→        then: SPA shows spec item detail for that ref\n   536→      - id: ac-14\n   537→        given: SPA renders\n   538→        when: validation data present in snapshot\n   539→        then: shows validation summary badge (green check or red X with count)\n   540→      - id: ac-15\n   541→        given: static export page\n   542→        when: displayed to user\n   543→        then: \"shows 'Data as of: [timestamp]' indicator prominently\"\n   544→      - id: ac-16\n   545→        given: viewing task in SPA mode\n   546→        when: user sees Start Task button area\n   547→        then: button is disabled with tooltip explaining read-only mode\n   548→      - id: ac-17\n   549→        given: viewing inbox in SPA mode\n   550→        when: Add button area visible\n   551→        then: button is disabled/hidden\n   552→      - id: ac-18\n   553→        given: SPA mode\n   554→        when: any write action attempted\n   555→        then: graceful no-op with informative message\n   556→  - _ulid: 01KFMM8F5WG89H244FXVSRZ35E\n   557→    slugs:\n   558→      - cli-serve-commands\n   559→    title: CLI Serve Commands\n   560→    type: feature\n   561→    tags:\n   562→      - cli\n   563→      - serve\n   564→    description: |\n   565→      CLI commands for managing the daemon server lifecycle. Provides human and script-friendly\n   566→      interfaces to start, stop, and monitor the daemon.\n   567→    depends_on:\n   568→      - \"@daemon-server\"\n   569→    implements: []\n   570→    relates_to: []\n   571→    tests: []\n   572→    traits:\n   573→      - \"@trait-json-output\"\n   574→      - \"@trait-semantic-exit-codes\"\n   575→      - \"@trait-error-guidance\"\n   576→    notes: []\n   577→    created: 2026-01-22T07:00:00.000Z\n   578→    acceptance_criteria:\n   579→      - id: ac-1\n   580→        given: daemon not running\n   581→        when: kspec serve executed\n   582→        then: starts server in foreground, logs to stdout, Ctrl+C stops\n   583→      - id: ac-2\n   584→        given: daemon not running\n   585→        when: kspec serve --daemon executed\n   586→        then: starts in background, writes PID file, returns immediately with status message\n   587→      - id: ac-3\n   588→        given: daemon not running\n   589→        when: kspec serve --port 8080 executed\n   590→        then: starts on specified port\n   591→      - id: ac-4\n   592→        given: daemon running\n   593→        when: kspec serve stop executed\n   594→        then: sends SIGTERM to daemon PID, waits for clean shutdown, removes PID file\n   595→      - id: ac-5\n   596→        given: daemon not running\n   597→        when: kspec serve stop executed\n   598→        then: outputs 'Daemon not running' with exit code 0 (idempotent)\n   599→      - id: ac-6\n   600→        given: any state\n   601→        when: kspec serve status executed\n   602→        then: outputs JSON with {running, pid, port, uptime, connections}\n   603→      - id: ac-7\n   604→        given: daemon running\n   605→        when: kspec serve restart executed\n   606→        then: stops existing daemon, starts new one, preserves port setting\n   607→      - id: ac-8\n   608→        given: any state\n   609→        when: kspec serve logs executed\n   610→        then: tails daemon log file (.kspec/.daemon.log)\n   611→      - id: ac-9\n   612→        given: daemon running\n   613→        when: kspec serve logs --follow executed\n   614→        then: streams log output continuously until Ctrl+C\n   615→      - id: ac-10\n   616→        given: port already in use\n   617→        when: kspec serve attempts to start\n   618→        then: fails with clear error message suggesting --port flag\n   619→    status:\n   620→      maturity: draft\n   621→      implementation: implemented\n   622→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n```"}}]}}}
