ach:**\n```typescript\n// AC: @daemon-server ac-16\nit('should compile standalone executable with bun build --compile', async () => {\n  const daemonDir = join(process.cwd(), 'packages/daemon');\n  \n  // Run build:compile\n  const buildResult = spawnSync('bun', ['run', 'build:compile'], {\n    cwd: daemonDir,\n    encoding: 'utf-8',\n  });\n  \n  expect(buildResult.exitCode).toBe(0);\n  \n  // Verify executable exists\n  const execPath = join(daemonDir, 'dist/kspec-daemon');\n  const stats = await stat(execPath);\n  expect(stats.isFile()).toBe(true);\n  expect(stats.mode & 0o111).toBeGreaterThan(0); // Executable bit\n  \n  // Verify it's an ELF binary (Linux) or appropriate format\n  const result = spawnSync('file', [execPath], { encoding: 'utf-8' });\n  expect(result.stdout).toMatch(/executable/i);\n  \n  // Verify standalone (should run without Bun - may fail but shouldn't require Bun)\n  const runResult = spawnSync(execPath, ['--help'], {\n    encoding: 'utf-8',\n    timeout: 5000,\n  });\n  // Even if it errors, it should at least execute (not require Bun)\n  expect(runResult.error?.code).not.toBe('ENOENT');\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Test Isolation - MUST-FIX\n\n**Status:** ❌ **NO TESTS TO ISOLATE**\n\nSince no tests exist, isolation cannot be assessed. When tests are added:\n- Build tests should run in temp directories OR\n- Clean up compiled artifacts in afterEach hooks\n- Do not rely on persistent build state\n\n---\n\n## 5. Implementation Verification (Manual)\n\nDespite missing automated tests, I verified the implementation **works correctly**:\n\n### Build Script Verification\n✅ `packages/daemon/package.json` - `build:compile` script added  \n✅ `scripts/build-executables.sh` - Cross-platform builds script created  \n✅ Executable compilation succeeds (97MB Linux x64 binary)  \n✅ Cross-platform builds succeed (Linux, macOS ARM64/x64, Windows x64)  \n✅ Binaries are actual executables (verified with `file` command)\n\n### Manual Test Results\n```bash\n# Single platform build\n$ cd packages/daemon && bun run build:compile\n✅ Creates dist/kspec-daemon (97MB ELF executable)\n\n# Cross-platform build\n$ bash scripts/build-executables.sh\n✅ Creates 4 executables:\n  - kspec-daemon-linux-x64 (97MB)\n  - kspec-daemon-darwin-arm64 (56MB)\n  - kspec-daemon-darwin-x64 (61MB)\n  - kspec-daemon-win-x64.exe (109MB)\n\n# Standalone verification\n$ file dist/kspec-daemon\n✅ ELF 64-bit LSB executable, dynamically linked\n```\n\n---\n\n## Blocking Issues Summary\n\n### MUST-FIX Before Merge\n\n1. **Missing AC-16 Test Coverage (BLOCKING)**\n   - Add automated test that validates `bun build --compile` produces working executable\n   - Test should verify executable exists, is executable, and can run standalone\n   - Must include `// AC: @daemon-server ac-16` annotation\n\n### Advisory Improvements\n\n2. **Test Strategy (Advisory)**\n   - Prefer E2E test over unit test (actually run the build, verify the output)\n   - Consider CI integration to catch build breakage early\n\n---\n\n## Conclusion\n\n**Verdict:** ❌ **NOT READY FOR MERGE**\n\nThe implementation is **functionally correct** and the feature works as specified in AC-16. However, the PR violates kspec's requirement that **every AC must have test coverage**. This is particularly important for build functionality, which can silently break and cause downstream issues.\n\n**Required action:** Add automated test coverage for AC-16 before merging.\n\n**Estimated effort:** 15-30 minutes to add E2E test using existing test patterns.\n\n---\n\n## Files Changed\n\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/package.json` - Added chmod for dist CLI\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/packages/daemon/package.json` - Added build:compile script\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/scripts/build-executables.sh` - Cross-platform build script (NEW)"}},{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"agentId: afd57fc (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)"}}]}}}
